{"number": 1, "anchor": "ADD_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.1a", "red": "RED_0001", "expected_red": ["constructor-unit-tests"], "red_in": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests"], "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [], "how_to": "Red first for 001 §B 'Physics is pure data' (.spec-md §3.1): a tabulated import becomes axis data. Facts only; no production file changes. In `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs` (module `MaterialImportTests`, beside the tabulated facts at `:35-59`) add three facts. (1) `a tabulated refractiveindex.info page imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range`: `(readYaml \"Si.yml\").importMaterial` MUST be `Ok entry` whose `entry.complexity` is `Some c` with `c.eps = EpsWithDispValue (IsotropicDispersive [ segment ])`, `c.magnetic = None` and `c.active = None`; `segment.wavelengthInterval.lower.value` and `.upper.value` MUST be the first and last tabulated wavelengths of `fixtures/Si.yml` (0.250 µm and 0.700 µm) in metres, within 1e-15 m; `c.isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:864`) MUST be false, because a table is not editable term data, and the import stays view-only as its `complexity = None` keeps it today (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:193`); and `entry.properties.epsWithDisp.getEps w` MUST equal `c.toProperties.epsWithDisp.getEps w` at every tabulated wavelength (the seed invariant `properties = complexity.toProperties`). The fact MUST NOT name an `EpsAxisDispersion` case that does not exist yet, so it compiles on the start tree. (2) `an n,k CSV imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range`: the same assertions over `(readCsv \"sample-nk.csv\").importMaterial` and its range, 400 nm to 700 nm. (3) `tabulated imports reproduce every sample and the linear interpolation between neighbours`: for every row of `Si.yml` and of `sample-nk.csv`, `epsAt entry` at the row's wavelength MUST equal `nkSquared` of the row's n and k, and at the midpoint of every pair of neighbouring rows it MUST equal `nkSquared` of the two rows' mean n and mean k, each within the file's `closeC 1e-12`. The fact writes the rows out from the fixtures; it does not parse the fixtures a second way. Facts (1) and (2) are red on the start tree, because `entryFromTabulated` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:183-194`) sets `complexity = None`. Fact (3) passes on the start tree's closure (`buildTabulatedClosure`, `:158-179`) and MUST stay green when the closure becomes data in step 2: it proves that no number moves.", "acceptance": "After the three facts land, constructor-unit-tests (MaterialImportTests) MUST fail with exactly `a tabulated refractiveindex.info page imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range` and `an n,k CSV imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range`, each failing on a `None` complexity; `tabulated imports reproduce every sample and the linear interpolation between neighbours` and every fact the class held before MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests.a tabulated refractiveindex.info page imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests.an n,k CSV imports as one view-only dispersive segment over its sample range", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests.tabulated imports reproduce every sample and the linear interpolation between neighbours", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 2, "anchor": "CLOSE_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.1a", "closes": "RED_0001", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [1], "how_to": "The tabulated n,k table becomes an axis case of the core, and the import builds it (001 §B; .spec-md §3.1). The kernel MOVES from Storage into the core in this step, so one implementation exists. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`, before `EpsAxisDispersion` (`:365`): (a) `TabulatedInterpolation`, a one-case union `LinearInWaveLengthClamped` (linear in λ, clamped to the end samples), with `member value : int` = 1 and `static member tryOfWire (v : int) : TabulatedInterpolation option` answering `None` for any other tag. (b) `TabulatedTableError` with `EmptyTableErr`, `SampleCountMismatchErr` and `UnsortedSamplesErr`, each `of reason : string` naming the counts or the first offending index. (c) `TabulatedNkTable`, a record marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier(\"...\")>]` with `wavelengths : float<meter> array` (ascending), `n : float array`, `k : float array` and `interpolation : TabulatedInterpolation`. `static member tryCreate (wavelengths : float<meter> array) (n : float array) (k : float array) : Result<TabulatedNkTable, TabulatedTableError>` refuses an empty table, columns of unequal length and a wavelength column that decreases anywhere, sets `interpolation = LinearInWaveLengthClamped`, and does not sort. `member sampleRange : WaveLengthInterval` answers the first to the last sample, each as `WaveLength.nm`. `member complexIndex (w : WaveLength) : ComplexRefractionIndex` is the arithmetic of `buildTabulatedClosure` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs:160-179`) moved verbatim, answering the index instead of its `Eps`: a one-sample table answers that sample; at or below the first sample, the first; at or above the last, the last; otherwise the same forward scan for the bracketing pair, with t = (λ − a)/(b − a) and t = 0 when the pair shares one wavelength. (d) `EpsAxisDispersion` gains `TabulatedNK of TabulatedNkTable`, and `complexIndex` (`:371-378`) calls the table. While the custom equality stays (until step 9), `Equals` (`:380-388`) compares two `TabulatedNK` values structurally and `GetHashCode` (`:390-394`) hashes the table structurally. The doc comment at `:346-356` names the new case. (2) Every match on `EpsAxisDispersion` follows the new case: `DispersionModel.parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:427-435`) answers `[]` for it, because a table has no editable term scalars; `EpsAxisDispersion.facetKey` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs:91-95`) answers `DiscreteKey \"Tabulated n/k\"`; and `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:864-871`) treats it as the evaluated case is treated, as data that is not editable term data. Their doc comments name the new case. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs`: `entryFromTabulated` (`:183-194`) sorts its rows by wavelength with the `Array.sortBy` `buildTabulatedClosure` used (`:159`), builds the table through `TabulatedNkTable.tryCreate`, and answers `Result<MaterialEntry, ImportError>`; a `TabulatedTableError` maps to `NoDataErr` carrying its reason. The entry's `complexity` is `Some` with one isotropic dispersive segment over `table.sampleRange` whose axis is `TabulatedNK table`, `magnetic = None` and `active = None`, and `properties = complexity.toProperties`, as `entryOfAxis` (`:455-469`) does for formula imports. The two call sites (`:502`, `:544`) drop their `Ok` wrapper. `buildTabulatedClosure` is deleted. The closure wording of the module doc (`:18-26`) and of `entryFromTabulated` (`:190-192`) is rewritten, and `NkTableRow`'s carrier reason (`:84`) no longer names a closure. Formula imports are untouched. A tabulated import now has a defined band, its sample range, so the out-of-band diagnostic flags a request outside it (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs:166-177`). This is intended: outside its range the table clamps. (4) Facts. `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs` gains five: `A tabulated axis returns each sample at its own wavelength and interpolates linearly between neighbours`, `A tabulated axis clamps to its first sample below the table and to its last sample above it`, `A single-sample tabulated axis is constant at every wavelength`, `TabulatedNkTable tryCreate refuses an empty table, unequal columns and a decreasing wavelength column` and `The tabulated interpolation rule round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag`. They use a hand-written table (for example 400, 500 and 700 nm, n 1.50, 1.60 and 1.90, k 0.00, 0.10 and 0.30), compute each expected value in the fact, and compare through `BerremanTests.MatrixComparison`'s helpers. The interpolating fact also builds the engine `Eps` through `EpsWithDispValue.toEpsWithDisp` and compares it with `Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex` of the interpolated index. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs` gains `a tabulated axis lands on the tabulated n,k facet key`. `MaterialImportTests` gains `the imported table holds the samples sorted by wavelength in metres under the linear clamped rule`, which matches `TabulatedNK table` on the `Si.yml` import and checks its three columns against the fixture rows. No number moves: step 1's facts are the proof.", "acceptance": "After the table becomes axis data, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the two MaterialImportTests facts step 1 left red, `tabulated imports reproduce every sample and the linear interpolation between neighbours`, the two new facts, and every other MaterialImportTests, LibraryFacetsTests and ExportImportTests fact; unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass with the five new tabulated facts; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.A tabulated axis returns each sample at its own wavelength and interpolates linearly between neighbours", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.A tabulated axis clamps to its first sample below the table and to its last sample above it", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.A single-sample tabulated axis is constant at every wavelength", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.TabulatedNkTable tryCreate refuses an empty table, unequal columns and a decreasing wavelength column", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The tabulated interpolation rule round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests.a tabulated axis lands on the tabulated n,k facet key", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests.the imported table holds the samples sorted by wavelength in metres under the linear clamped rule", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-TABULATED"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 3, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.1b", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalConstructor.Domain"], "depends_on": [], "how_to": "`AbscissaKind` MOVES from the Domain into the core, so the transcendental laws of steps 5 and 7 can carry their abscissa as data (.spec-md §3.1). No number moves and no behaviour changes. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`, after `ComplexDispersionFormula` (`:272-280`): the public union `AbscissaKind` with `LinearInX of wavelengthScale : float<meter>` and `ReciprocalInX of ReciprocalAbscissa`, and the record `ReciprocalAbscissa`, marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier(\"...\")>]`, with `wavelengthScale : float<meter>` and `numerator : float`. The doc comment of `OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:582-585` moves with it. (2) `DispersionModels.fs`: the private `AbscissaKind` (`:586-602`) is deleted. Its `ofUnit` becomes a static extension member of the core type, `static member ofUnit (u : UnitOfMeasure) : AbscissaKind`, declared in `DispersionModels.fs` before its first use, because it reads the `Units` seam and the core cannot reference it. Its body is unchanged, except that it builds the reciprocal case as `ReciprocalInX { wavelengthScale = nanometer; numerator = (fromMeters u nanometer).value }`. The five lowering sites that match it (`:697`, `:706`, `:723`, `:738`, `:753`) read `r.wavelengthScale` and `r.numerator` where they read `(scale, numerator)` and `numerator.value`. The `AC-B5` grid facts of `OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs` (`:181-298`), over micrometre and electron-volt abscissas, are the proof and stay unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the move, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with DispersionModelsTests' AC-B5 lowering facts unchanged; unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 4, "anchor": "ADD_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.1c", "red": "RED_0002", "expected_red": ["constructor-unit-tests"], "red_in": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests"], "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [3], "how_to": "Red first: an analytic model lowers to DATA, so equal models lower to equal axes (001 §B 'Physics is pure data'; .spec-md §3.1). Facts only. In `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs` add `equal Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models lower to equal axis data`. It uses the Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator coefficient sets of `AC-B5 transcendental models lower to the evaluated case and match evaluate` (`:306-326`). For each model, lowering it twice through `toEpsAxis`, and lowering two separately built equal models, MUST give equal `EpsAxisDispersion` values with equal hashes, and `toEpsValue` MUST give equal `EpsWithDispValue` values. A model whose `bandGap` (Tauc-Lorentz) or `energy` (Gaussian) differs MUST lower to an unequal axis. The fact is red on the start tree: both models lower to `EpsAxisEvaluated this.evaluate` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:766-769`), a fresh closure on every call, which the custom equality compares by reference (`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:386`).", "acceptance": "After the fact lands, constructor-unit-tests (DispersionModelsTests) MUST fail with exactly `equal Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models lower to equal axis data`, failing on the first equality of two lowered axes; every fact the class held before MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests.equal Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models lower to equal axis data", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 5, "anchor": "CLOSE_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.1c", "closes": "RED_0002", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [4], "how_to": "The Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models become axis data, evaluated by kernels that MOVE into the core, so one implementation exists (.spec-md §3.1). (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`: (a) `AbscissaKind` gains `member abscissaAt (w : WaveLength) : float`: `LinearInX scale` answers `w.value / scale`, and `ReciprocalInX r` answers `r.numerator / (w.value / r.wavelengthScale)`. For every `UnitOfMeasure` this is the same floating-point arithmetic as `fromMeters` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/Units.fs:104-114`) over the scale and numerator `ofUnit` derives, so the abscissa is bit-identical. (b) Two records marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier(\"...\")>]`: `TaucLorentzLaw` (`epsInf`, `amplitude`, `resonance`, `broadening`, `bandGap`, `abscissa : AbscissaKind`) and `GaussianOscillatorLaw` (`epsInf`, `amplitude`, `energy`, `broadening`, `abscissa : AbscissaKind`). Each has `member complexIndex (w : WaveLength) : ComplexRefractionIndex`, whose body is its arm of `baseIndex` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:508-517`) moved verbatim over `x = this.abscissa.abscissaAt w`. (c) `EpsAxisDispersion` gains `TaucLorentzAxis of TaucLorentzLaw` and `GaussianOscillatorAxis of GaussianOscillatorLaw`. `complexIndex` calls the law, and the custom `Equals` / `GetHashCode` compare and hash both structurally. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs`: `TaucLorentzCoefficients` and `GaussianOscillatorCoefficients` gain `member toTaucLorentzLaw : TaucLorentzLaw` and `member toGaussianOscillatorLaw : GaussianOscillatorLaw`. Each copies the coefficients and takes `abscissa = AbscissaKind.ofUnit this.wavelengthUnit`. `thermoOptic` is not carried, because lowering stays isothermal: `evaluateAt` (`:552-559`) still adds the correction on top of `baseIndex`. `baseIndex`'s two arms answer the law's index, and their bodies are deleted there. `toEpsAxis` (`:766-769`) lowers `TaucLorentz c` to `TaucLorentzAxis c.toTaucLorentzLaw` and `GaussianOscillator c` to `GaussianOscillatorAxis c.toGaussianOscillatorLaw`; `ForouhiBloomer` and `BrendelBormann` still lower to the evaluated case until step 7. `parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm (`:427-435`) answers `[]` for both new cases. The doc comments of `baseIndex`, `toEpsAxis`, `toEpsValue` and `toOpticalProperties` (`:485-489`, `:669-686`, `:763-765`, `:793-812`) say that these two models lower to their law. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs` `facetKey` (`:91-95`) maps both new cases to the existing `DiscreteKey \"Evaluated (transcendental)\"`, so `every DispersionModel kind lands on the vocabulary key its lowering denotes` (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs:464-482`) stays green unchanged. `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:864-871`) treats both as data that is not editable term data, as today. (4) Facts. `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs` gains `The Tauc-Lorentz law reproduces its reference index on both sides of the band gap`, `The Tauc-Lorentz law over a micrometre abscissa reproduces its reference index` and `The Gaussian-oscillator law reproduces its reference index`. They build the laws directly in the core. The first and third use the Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian sets of `DispersionModelsTests.fs:306-326` over the electron-volt abscissa `ReciprocalInX { wavelengthScale = 1.0e-9<meter>; numerator = 1239.84 }`. The second uses a Tauc-Lorentz set over `LinearInX 1.0e-6<meter>` whose band gap lies between 0.3 µm and 2.0 µm. Each compares `complexIndex` at 300, 450, 600, 900 and 2000 nm, with exact `Assert.Equal`, against G17 literals the worker records from the start tree's `DispersionModel.evaluate` before moving the arms. In `DispersionModelsTests.fs`, `AC-B5 transcendental models lower to the evaluated case and match evaluate` (`:300-337`) matches each model's own law case where it matched `EpsAxisEvaluated _`, and `AC-B5 toEpsValue short-circuits ConstantNK and builds a single-segment tree otherwise` (`:380-382`) matches `TaucLorentzAxis _`. Their exact `Assert.Equal((f w).value, (axis.complexIndex w).value)` and 1e-12 assertions are unchanged, and their comments (`:302-305`, `:378-379`) no longer name `EpsAxisEvaluated`.", "acceptance": "After the two laws land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `equal Tauc-Lorentz and Gaussian-oscillator models lower to equal axis data` (red since step 4), with DispersionModelsTests' AC-B6 reference facts and LibraryFacetsTests unchanged; unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass, with the three new law facts equal to their literals; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The Tauc-Lorentz law reproduces its reference index on both sides of the band gap", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The Tauc-Lorentz law over a micrometre abscissa reproduces its reference index", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The Gaussian-oscillator law reproduces its reference index", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests.AC-B5 transcendental models lower to the evaluated case and match evaluate", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests.AC-B5 toEpsValue short-circuits ConstantNK and builds a single-segment tree otherwise", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 6, "anchor": "ADD_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.1d", "red": "RED_0003", "expected_red": ["constructor-unit-tests"], "red_in": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests"], "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [5], "how_to": "Red first, as in step 4, for the two remaining transcendental models (001 §B; .spec-md §3.1). Facts only. In `Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs` add `equal Forouhi-Bloomer and Brendel-Bormann models lower to equal axis data`. Lowering `forouhiBloomerASi` and `brendelBormannGold` (`:403-430`) twice each, and lowering a separately built equal copy of each, MUST give equal `toEpsAxis` values with equal hashes and equal `toEpsValue` values. A copy whose `bandGap` (Forouhi-Bloomer) or first `broadening` (Brendel-Bormann) differs MUST lower to an unequal axis. The fact is red on the tree step 5 leaves: both models still lower to `EpsAxisEvaluated this.evaluate`, which the custom equality compares by reference (`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:386`).", "acceptance": "After the fact lands, constructor-unit-tests (DispersionModelsTests) MUST fail with exactly `equal Forouhi-Bloomer and Brendel-Bormann models lower to equal axis data`, failing on the first equality of two lowered axes; every fact the class held before MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests.equal Forouhi-Bloomer and Brendel-Bormann models lower to equal axis data", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 7, "anchor": "CLOSE_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.1d", "closes": "RED_0003", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [6], "how_to": "The Forouhi-Bloomer and Brendel-Bormann models become axis data, so no model lowers to the evaluated case (.spec-md §3.1). (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`: `ForouhiBloomerLaw` (`nInf`, `a`, `b`, `c`, `bandGap`, `abscissa`) and `BrendelBormannLaw` (`plasmaFrequency`, `intrabandStrength`, `intrabandDamping`, then `strength`, `resonance`, `damping` and `broadening` as `float list`, then `abscissa`), marked `[<Softellect.Sys.NumericCarrier(\"...\")>]`. Each has a `complexIndex` whose body is its arm of `baseIndex` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:518-538`) moved verbatim over `this.abscissa.abscissaAt w`. Weideman's Faddeeva series (`faddeevaTermCount`, `FaddeevaSeries`, `faddeevaSeries` and `faddeeva`, `:437-483`) moves into `Dispersion.fs` beside `BrendelBormannLaw`, stays private there, and is deleted from the Domain. `EpsAxisDispersion` gains `ForouhiBloomerAxis of ForouhiBloomerLaw` and `BrendelBormannAxis of BrendelBormannLaw`, with `complexIndex`, `Equals` and `GetHashCode` arms as in step 5. (2) `DispersionModels.fs`: `ForouhiBloomerCoefficients.toForouhiBloomerLaw` and `BrendelBormannCoefficients.toBrendelBormannLaw`, built as step 5's members are. `baseIndex`'s two arms answer the law's index. `toEpsAxis` lowers both models to their cases, so its `EpsAxisEvaluated this.evaluate` line (`:766-769`) is gone and every model lowers to data. `parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm answers `[]` for both cases. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs` maps both cases to `DiscreteKey \"Evaluated (transcendental)\"`, and `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:864-871`) treats both as data that is not editable term data. (4) Facts. `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs` gains `The Forouhi-Bloomer law reproduces its reference index on both sides of the band gap` and `The Brendel-Bormann law reproduces its reference index`. They use the `forouhiBloomerASi` and `brendelBormannGold` sets (`DispersionModelsTests.fs:403-430`) over the electron-volt abscissa, at 300, 450, 600, 900 and 2000 nm, exact against G17 literals recorded from the pre-move `DispersionModel.evaluate`. Three arms that matched `EpsAxisEvaluated _` follow the law cases: `AC-B6 ForouhiBloomer and BrendelBormann lower to the evaluated case and match evaluate` (`DispersionModelsTests.fs:534-552`); `step 015: a transcendental dispersive segment derives and evaluates without rejection` (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs:321-340`), which also asserts `Assert.False(c.isEditable)`, pinning the unchanged view-only behaviour; and `ForouhiBloomer and BrendelBormann are pickable and lower to the evaluated segment` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs:305-317`). Their other assertions are unchanged, and their comments no longer name `EpsAxisEvaluated`.", "acceptance": "After the two laws land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `equal Forouhi-Bloomer and Brendel-Bormann models lower to equal axis data` (red since step 6), with DispersionModelsTests' AC-B6 reference facts unchanged; unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass, with the two new law facts equal to their literals; ui-tests (MaterialEditorWindowTests) and ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The Forouhi-Bloomer law reproduces its reference index on both sides of the band gap", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The Brendel-Bormann law reproduces its reference index", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests.AC-B6 ForouhiBloomer and BrendelBormann lower to the evaluated case and match evaluate", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.step 015: a transcendental dispersive segment derives and evaluates without rejection", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.ForouhiBloomer and BrendelBormann are pickable and lower to the evaluated segment", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S11-OSCILLATORS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 8, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.1e", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalProperties", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests"], "depends_on": [], "how_to": "The built-in Silicon and Langasite carry their dispersion as data. This section's brief does not name them, but their complexities hold `EpsAxisEvaluated` closures (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:455`, `:476-477`). Step 9 deletes that case, so they must become data first, and 001 §A ships them as catalogue files. Their indices are the engine's published closed forms (`Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs`), not finite term sums: Silicon's k is a ratio of polynomials, and Langasite's k is a Gaussian in λ. They become a closed set of published laws. The kernels MOVE into the core from `Dispersive.fs`, and the re-statements in `MaterialLibrary.fs` (`:422-447`) are deleted, so each closed form exists once. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`: `PublishedIndexLaw` with `SiliconIndexLaw`, `LangasiteOrdinaryIndexLaw` and `LangasiteExtraordinaryIndexLaw`, with `member value : int` (1, 2, 3), `static member tryOfWire (v : int) : PublishedIndexLaw option` (`None` for any other tag) and `member complexIndex (w : WaveLength) : ComplexRefractionIndex`. The arms of `complexIndex` are the closed forms of `Dispersive.fs` moved verbatim: Silicon's `nSi`, `xiSiFinal` and `refrIndexSi` (`:78-87`), and Langasite's `refrIndexLa3Ga5SiO14Ordinary` and `refrIndexLa3Ga5SiO14ExtraOrdinary` (`:27-37`, with `numberE = exp 1.0` from `:22`). `EpsAxisDispersion` gains `PublishedLawAxis of PublishedIndexLaw`, with `complexIndex`, `Equals` and `GetHashCode` arms. (2) `Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs`: `Silicon`'s eps is `Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex` of `SiliconIndexLaw.complexIndex`, and its three lets are deleted. `Langasite`'s `epsLa3Ga5SiO14` (`:51-55`) reads the two Langasite laws. `g11La3Ga5SiO14` and `g33La3Ga5SiO14` (`:40-49`) read the real parts of the two laws' indices where they re-state those expressions, and the two index lets are deleted. Every preset number is unchanged, because the same expressions are evaluated. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs`: `siliconComplexity` (`:453-458`) carries `PublishedLawAxis SiliconIndexLaw`, and `langasiteComplexity` (`:469-481`) carries `PublishedLawAxis LangasiteOrdinaryIndexLaw` and `PublishedLawAxis LangasiteExtraordinaryIndexLaw`. The private re-statements `siliconRefractionIndex`, `langasiteOrdinaryIndex` and `langasiteExtraordinaryIndex` (`:422-447`) are deleted. The coded-preset comment block (`:388-411`), the doc of `codedPresetInterval` (`:413-418`) and both complexities' docs (`:449-452`, `:460-468`) are rewritten: the dispersion is the published law the engine preset evaluates, and no closure remains, so the file no longer names `EpsAxisEvaluated`. (4) The matches follow the case. `parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:427-435`) answers `[]`. `facetKey` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs:91-95`) answers `DiscreteKey \"Evaluated (transcendental)\"`, so Silicon's facet key is unchanged (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs:492`). `isEditable` treats the case as data that is not editable term data, so Silicon stays view-only (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs:480-484`). (5) Facts in `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs`: `The silicon published law reproduces the engine Silicon index` and `The langasite published laws reproduce the engine Langasite ordinary and extraordinary indices`. Each compares the law's `complexIndex` at 400, 500, 600, 800 and 1000 nm, with exact `Assert.Equal`, against G17 literals the worker records from the start tree's closures before moving them. Each also compares the engine preset's `getEps` (`siliconOpticalProperties` / `langasiteOpticalProperties`) with `Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex` of those literals, through `MatrixComparison`. A third fact, `The published index law round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag`, covers the tags. The constructor facts that pin Silicon and Langasite to the engine presets stay unchanged and green: `the silicon library entry reproduces the engine Silicon preset bit-for-bit` (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs:48-55`) and `the re-seeded silicon and langasite eps reproduce the engine presets` (`OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs:151-161`).", "acceptance": "After the published laws land, unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass, with the three new facts and the laws equal to their literals; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, with the Silicon and Langasite reproduction facts and LibraryFacetsTests unchanged; ui-tests (MaterialsWindowTests, FsxAcceptanceTests) and ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The silicon published law reproduces the engine Silicon index", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-PUBLISHED-LAWS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The langasite published laws reproduce the engine Langasite ordinary and extraordinary indices", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-PUBLISHED-LAWS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.The published index law round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-PUBLISHED-LAWS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 9, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.1f", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [2, 7, 8], "how_to": "`EpsAxisEvaluated` and the custom equality are deleted, so every axis is data and `EpsAxisDispersion` takes F#'s structural equality (001 §B; .spec-md §0.1, first row). After steps 2, 5, 7 and 8, nothing produces the case. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`: delete `EpsAxisEvaluated` (`:369`), its `complexIndex` arm, `[<CustomEquality; NoComparison>]` (`:365`) and the `Equals` / `GetHashCode` overrides (`:380-394`). The doc comment above `RealNkFormulas` (`:346-356`) moves above `EpsAxisDispersion` and lists its data cases: term data (`RealNK`, `ComplexEps`), the tabulated table, the four oscillator laws and the published laws. (2) The dead arms are deleted: `parameters`' `SumOfTerms` arm (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:433-435`), `facetKey` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs:95`) and `isEditable` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:867`). `isEditable`'s predicate then reads: an axis is editable exactly when it is `RealNK` or `ComplexEps` term data. Every doc comment that names the evaluated closure is rewritten: `DispersionModels.fs`' module doc (`:10-23`) and the docs of `toEpsAxis`, `toEpsValue` and `toOpticalProperties`; `LibraryFacets.fs:82-90` and `:99-104`; and `MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:854-863`. (3) The two out-of-band fixtures build a flat data axis where they built `EpsAxisEvaluated (fun _ -> …)`: `OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs:37-38` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs:52-53`. The axis is a constant `RealNK` with n = 1.5 and k = 0, because the diagnostic reads only the segment intervals. (4) `Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs` gains `Equal axis data of every case is equal and hashes equal, and a changed value breaks equality`. For `RealNK`, `ComplexEps`, `TabulatedNK`, the four law cases and `PublishedLawAxis`, two separately built equal values MUST be equal with equal hashes, and changing one coefficient, sample or law MUST make them unequal. (5) Afterwards no file under `Berreman/` names `EpsAxisEvaluated`, in code or in a comment. S1.2's invariant `s02-no-eps-axis-evaluated` greps for it from S1.2's first step on.", "acceptance": "After the case is deleted, unit-tests (EpsWithDispValueTests, DispersionFormulaTests) MUST pass with the structural-equality fact; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-tests (OutOfBandBadgeTests, MaterialEditorWindowTests, MaterialsWindowTests) and ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the three s01 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.DispersionFormulaTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests.Equal axis data of every case is equal and hashes equal, and a changed value breaks equality", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/EpsWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S11-NO-CLOSURE"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.1 -- Every dispersion axis is data: tabulated and transcendental cases"}
{"number": 10, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.2a", "touches": ["Berreman", "OpticalProperties", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "BerremanTests", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [8, 9], "how_to": "Langasite's dispersive gyration becomes data, so that the engine Langasite preset can be stated as a `MaterialComplexity` once step 13 derives `properties` from the complexity (001 §B 'Physics is pure data'; .spec-md §3.2). The section brief does not name it; the deviation is recorded in `.history`. `FsxAcceptanceTests` stores the engine preset itself as a library material (`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs:386`) and compares the table with `LangasiteOnSilicon.fsx`, whose film is that preset (`Berreman/Analytics/StandardSystems.fs:40-53`). `RhoWithDispValue` (`Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs:RhoWithDispValue`) carries only `DispersionFormula` components, while the preset's ρ (`Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs:58-63`, `rhoLa3Ga5SiO14`) is diag(i·g₁₁(λ), 0, i·g₃₃(λ)) with the transcendental g₁₁ and g₃₃ of `:40-49`. The kernels MOVE into the core, as S1.1 step 8 moved the index laws, so one implementation exists. (1) `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`, after `GyrotropicValue` and before `RhoWithDispValue`: `PublishedGyrationLaw`, a one-case union `LangasiteGyrationLaw` with `member value : int` = 1, `static member tryOfWire (v : int) : PublishedGyrationLaw option` (`None` for any other tag) and `member rhoAt (w : WaveLength) : Rho`. Its body is `g11La3Ga5SiO14`, `g33La3Ga5SiO14` and `rhoLa3Ga5SiO14` moved verbatim, reading the two Langasite `PublishedIndexLaw` cases as step 8 left those lets. `RhoWithDispValue` gains `PublishedLawRho of PublishedGyrationLaw`, and its doc names the case. (2) `Berreman/OpticalProperties/Active.fs:146-156`: `toRhoWithDisp` answers `RhoWithDisp law.rhoAt` for the case, and its doc says so. (3) `Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs`: `Langasite`'s `rhoWithDisp` (`:70`) is `RhoWithDisp LangasiteGyrationLaw.rhoAt`, and the three lets are deleted. Every engine number is unchanged, because the same expressions are evaluated. (4) Every match follows the case. A published law is data the editor ladder cannot carry. `MaterialComplexityEditError` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:182-187`) gains `PublishedGyrationNotEditableErr of reason : string`. `ofComplexity`'s active arm answers it, naming the law, and its `caption` arm is added at `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:372-375`. `MaterialComplexity.isEditable` (`MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:MaterialComplexity.isEditable`) answers false when the active aspect is a published law, so such an entry opens view-only. The gyration-class and handedness facets (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs:materialGyrationClassDef`, `materialHandednessDef`) still apply to it but extract no value, because a published law has no editor class and no handedness field. `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs:164-167`) answers `allGyrationComponents` for it. (5) The built-in Langasite keeps the constant uniaxial gyration its seed carries, so no library number moves. The doc of `langasiteComplexity` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:langasiteComplexity`) says so and names the published law as the engine preset's ρ. The comment at `OpticalConstructor.Tests/PropagationTests.fs:464-469` no longer says the ρ has no value-tree form. (6) Facts. `Berreman/BerremanTests/RhoWithDispValueTests.fs` gains two. `The langasite gyration law reproduces the engine Langasite rho`: at 400, 500, 600, 800 and 1000 nm, Im ρ₁₁ and Im ρ₃₃ of `LangasiteGyrationLaw.rhoAt` MUST equal, with exact `Assert.Equal`, G17 literals the worker records from `rhoLa3Ga5SiO14` before moving it; every other entry and every real part MUST be zero; and `(PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw).toRhoWithDisp.getRho w` and `langasiteOpticalProperties.rhoWithDisp.getRho w` MUST equal `rhoAt w` through `MatrixComparison`. `The published gyration law round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag` covers the tag. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs` gains `a published gyration law keeps a complexity view-only and refuses to seed the editor`: for a constant isotropic eps with `active = Some (PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw)`, `isEditable` MUST be false and `ofComplexity` MUST be `Error (PublishedGyrationNotEditableErr _)`. `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs` gains `a published gyration law offers the activity facets but extracts no class or handedness`, over an entry built by `materialEntryWith` (`:85-93`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs` gains `a published gyration law opens the editor view-only`: `initMaterialEditor` over such an entry MUST give `ViewOnlyMaterial _`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs` gains `a published gyration law draws every gyration component`: `gyrationComponentsOfComplexity` of that complexity MUST equal `allGyrationComponents`.", "acceptance": "After the gyration law lands, unit-tests (RhoWithDispValueTests, EpsWithDispValueTests) MUST pass with the two new facts and the law equal to its literals; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with the MaterialComplexityTests and LibraryFacetsTests facts; ui-tests (MaterialEditorWindowTests, NkDispersionChartTests, FsxAcceptanceTests) MUST pass with the two new facts and both LangasiteOnSilicon facts; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "unit-tests", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "unit-tests", "values": ["BerremanTests.RhoWithDispValueTests", "BerremanTests.EpsWithDispValueTests"]}, "constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs", "Berreman/OpticalProperties/Active.fs", "Berreman/OpticalProperties/Dispersive.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs", "Berreman/BerremanTests/RhoWithDispValueTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PropagationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.RhoWithDispValueTests.The langasite gyration law reproduces the engine Langasite rho", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/RhoWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.RhoWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "unit-tests", "id": "BerremanTests.RhoWithDispValueTests.The published gyration law round-trips its wire tag and refuses an unknown tag", "path": "Berreman/BerremanTests/RhoWithDispValueTests.fs", "class": "BerremanTests.RhoWithDispValueTests", "discovery_gate": "unit-tests", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.a published gyration law keeps a complexity view-only and refuses to seed the editor", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests.a published gyration law offers the activity facets but extracts no class or handedness", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryFacetsTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.a published gyration law opens the editor view-only", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests.a published gyration law draws every gyration component", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "Berreman.Dispersion.RhoWithDispValue", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialComplexityEditor.MaterialComplexityEditError", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S12-GYRATION-LAW"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.2 -- A material's physics is its complexity"}
{"number": 11, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.2b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [10], "how_to": "Every place that builds a `MaterialEntry` from engine properties states its physics as `MaterialComplexity` data first, while `properties` is still a field (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialEntry`). The script comparisons then prove that no number moves before step 13 changes the record (.spec-md §3.2). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs`: `material` (`:85-88`) takes a `MaterialComplexity` and saves `properties = complexity.toProperties` with the complexity. Each caller passes the script's material as data, and the script side keeps the script's own properties. `constantN 1.78052` (`:273`) becomes `EpsWithoutDispValue (IsotropicTransparent (RefractionIndex 1.78052))`. `dispersiveGlass` (`:357`; the script's n² = 1 + Σ bᵢλ²/(λ² − cᵢ) in µm, `:344-353`) becomes one isotropic dispersive segment over 300–700 nm whose axis is the Domain Sellmeier lowering `(Sellmeier { b = [ 1.43; 0.65 ]; c = [ 0.073 * 0.073; 0.12 * 0.12 ]; wavelengthUnit = Micrometer; thermoOptic = None }).toEpsAxis` (`OpticalConstructor.Domain/DispersionModels.fs:DispersionModel.toEpsAxis`). `langasiteOpticalProperties` (`:386`) becomes one uniaxial dispersive segment over 250–600 nm with `PublishedLawAxis LangasiteOrdinaryIndexLaw` and `PublishedLawAxis LangasiteExtraordinaryIndexLaw`, and `active = Some (PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw)` (step 10). `siliconOpticalProperties` (`:387`) becomes one isotropic dispersive segment over 250–600 nm with `PublishedLawAxis SiliconIndexLaw`. The glasses and the vacuum spacer (`:410-411`, `:442-443`) become `IsotropicTransparent` of `RefractionIndex.transparentGlass`, `RefractionIndex.vacuum`, `RefractionIndex.transparentGlass175` and `RefractionIndex.transparentGlass150`. For the EUV layers, `euvStack`, `euvAgainstIncidence` and `euvAgainstWaveLength` (`:477-509`) take each layer as a `ComplexRefractionIndex`. The table stores `IsotropicAbsorbing` of it, and the script's system builds it as the scripts do: `Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex`, then `OpticalProperties.fromEpsion` (`Berreman/OpticalProperties/Standard.fs:91`, `:110`). The EUV.fsx facts pass 1 − δ + iβ from `Eps.euvMolybdenumDelta` / `Eps.euvMolybdenumBeta` and `Eps.euvSiliconDelta` / `Eps.euvSiliconBeta`, and the EUV__002 facts pass their own (0.100, 0.045) and (0.006, 0.002); `euvComplex` (`:492-494`) is deleted. Every magnetic aspect is `None`, and so is every active aspect except Langasite's. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs`, `a minted MaterialId round-trips create-store-lookup through the library` (`:141-160`): the entry carries a constant `IsotropicTransparent (RefractionIndex 1.5)` complexity with `properties = complexity.toProperties`. The lookup assertion compares the resolved `getEps` at 400, 600 and 800 nm with the complexity's own, through the file's `epsClose 1e-12` (`:28`), not by reference, because step 13 derives `properties` on every read. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs`: `vacuumProperties` (`:46-56`) becomes `vacuumPlaceholderComplexity : MaterialComplexity` = `{ eps = EpsWithoutDispValue (IsotropicAbsorbing (ComplexRefractionIndex (Complex.create 1.0 0.0))); magnetic = None; active = None }`. Its composition is the same `Eps.fromComplexRefractionIndex` of 1 + 0i under the vacuum μ and ρ. `dtoToEntry` (`:93-111`) sets `properties` from it and carries it as the complexity, and the 'view-only until the §D.9 mapping lands' comment (`:106-107`) is deleted. Such an entry is now vacuum term data, editable like any constant material. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs` gains `a metadata-only library file re-imports each entry as vacuum data`. It exports the described `builtInEntries` (filtered as `:96-98` filters them) to a file under the test run's output directory and re-imports it; every imported entry's `complexity` MUST equal the vacuum value of (3).", "acceptance": "After every fixture states its physics as data, ui-tests (FsxAcceptanceTests) MUST pass, with every script comparison within its 1e-6 tolerance; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with the new ExportImportTests fact and the reworked minted-id fact; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExportImportTests.a metadata-only library file re-imports each entry as vacuum data", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExportImportTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.ExportImportTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S12-DATA-FIXTURES"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.DispersionModelsTests.a minted MaterialId round-trips create-store-lookup through the library", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "obligations": ["S12-DATA-FIXTURES"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.2 -- A material's physics is its complexity"}
{"number": 12, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.2c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Controls", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [], "how_to": "The view-only Edit gating of the domain-free materials control is deleted, with nothing replacing it (.spec-md §3.2). Its stated purpose was the `complexity = None` built-ins (`OpticalConstructor.Controls/MaterialsControls.fs:27-29`), and no product view hosts the control: `materialsControlsView` is mounted only by `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsControlsTests.fs:154` and `:190`. The Materials window keeps its own gate, `MaterialsWindowModel.editableSelection` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs:258-264`), which reads `MaterialComplexity.isEditable`. (1) `MaterialsControls.fs`: delete `MaterialEditability` (`:32-36`) and `MaterialsControlsRow.editability` (`:44`). `verbRow` (`:213-235`) always lists the Edit verb, offered on a selection exactly as Remove and View are. The module doc's view-only sentences (`:27-29`) and `verbRow`'s doc clause on Edit (`:213-215`) are deleted. The verb row's membership no longer changes, so `verbButton` drops `withKey` and its comment (`:157-159`). (2) `MaterialsControlsTests.fs`: `knownRows` (`:26-33`) lose `editability`, and their doc loses the view-only row; `matchesId`'s doc (`:20-22`) loses the Edit-removal example. The fact `a view-only selection carries no Edit affordance — the button is removed, not greyed` (`:183-201`) becomes `every selected row offers the Edit verb and a click dispatches editMaterial`: with the silicon row selected, the Edit verb MUST be present and a click on it MUST record the edit handler's tag, as `recorder` (`:60`) records the others.", "acceptance": "After the gating is deleted, ui-smoke MUST pass with `every selected row offers the Edit verb and a click dispatches editMaterial` in place of the view-only fact; ui-tests (MaterialsControlsTests) MUST pass; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Controls/MaterialsControls.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsControlsTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "migrate", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests.a view-only selection carries no Edit affordance — the button is removed, not greyed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsControlsTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests.every selected row offers the Edit verb and a click dispatches editMaterial", "obligations": ["S12-CONTROLS-EDIT"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.MaterialsControls.MaterialEditability", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S12-CONTROLS-EDIT"], "preserves_obligations": ["S12-CONTROLS-EDIT"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Controls.MaterialsControls.MaterialsControlsRow.editability", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S12-CONTROLS-EDIT"], "preserves_obligations": ["S12-CONTROLS-EDIT"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.2 -- A material's physics is its complexity"}
{"number": 13, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.2d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [10, 11, 12], "how_to": "`MaterialEntry.complexity` becomes mandatory, and `properties` becomes a member computed from it (001 §B; .spec-md §0.1 'MaterialLibrary.fs' row, §3.2). After steps 10 and 11 every construction already sets `properties = complexity.toProperties` with a present complexity. The record and all its consumers change in this one step, so the build stays green. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs:MaterialEntry`: the field `properties` is deleted, and `complexity : MaterialComplexity` replaces the option. The record gains `member this.properties : OpticalPropertiesWithDisp = this.complexity.toProperties`, so its readers (`resolveMaterialWithDisp`, `MaterialEntry.dispersion`, `Propagation.fs`, the views and the tests) keep compiling unchanged. Its doc says the complexity is the entry's physics and `properties` its engine composition. `builtInEntries` drops each `properties = …` line and each `Some`. Every field is now data, so `MaterialEntry` gains F#'s structural equality. (2) Every other construction drops `properties = …` and `Some`: `OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs` (`entryFromTabulated`, `entryOfAxis`), `OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs` `dtoToEntry` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs` `entryUnder` (`:416-424`). So do the fixtures: `LibraryFacetsTests.fs` `materialEntryWith`, the dispersive fixture of `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs`, `OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs` `dispersiveMaterial` (`:64-72`), the minted-id fact of `DispersionModelsTests.fs`, `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs` `material` and the step-10 fact of `MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`. The copy-and-updates `MaterialProxyTests.fs:52` and `SampleProxyTests.fs:487` keep only `complexity = …`. (3) Every reader of the option reads the value, and every `None` arm that stood for a coded, view-only preset is deleted with nothing replacing it. `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs`: `payloadOf` (`:76-80`) is `VersionPayload<MaterialComplexity, MaterialMetadata>` and compares the complexity directly, and the `MaterialMetadata` doc (`:28-34`) drops its coded-preset sentences. `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs`: the four private entry members (`constantEpsOpt`, `dispersiveEpsOpt`, `activeOpt`, `magneticOpt`) and the anisotropy facet read `entry.complexity`, and the anisotropy doc's defensive-`None` sentence goes. `OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs:84-90`: `ofEntry` is `ReachableMaterial.definedSegmentsOf entry.complexity`. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs`: `previewAnisotropy` (`:101-110`) is deleted, and its callers `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs:1114` and `:1151` read `shownEntry.complexity.anisotropy`. The docs that describe the coded-preset fallback or name `previewAnisotropy` (`NkDispersionChart.fs:156-163`, `:170-175`, `:208-211`; `MaterialEditorView.fs:266-270`) are rewritten: every component is drawn when a complexity names no gyration class. `MaterialsWindowView.fs`: `editableSelection` (`:253-264`) and the view panel's editability (`:1115-1120`) read `isEditable` off the complexity, and the caption ` (view-only engine preset)` becomes ` (view-only)`. `OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs:MaterialComplexity.isEditable`: its doc no longer contrasts the gate with complexity presence. (4) `MaterialEditorView.fs`: the view-only case carries the complexity it shows, `ViewOnlyMaterial of reason : ControlCaption * shown : MaterialComplexity` (`:64-69`). The fields `presetProperties` and `viewOnlyComplexity` (`:147-152`) are deleted. `previewProperties`, `previewGyrationComponents` and `previewMuKind` (`:256-290`) read `shown`, so their `None` arms go. `initMaterialEditor` (`:321-387`) seeds an editable entry through `ofComplexity`, whose `Error e` gives `ViewOnlyMaterial (e.caption, entry.complexity)`. Any other entry opens as `ViewOnlyMaterial (ControlCaption \"this entry's physics is not editable term data — view-only\", entry.complexity)`. The binders at `:411` and `:1289` take `(reason, _)`, and `complexitySummary`'s view-only caption (`:295`) becomes `view-only`. The module doc (`:1-20`), the `EditorMode` doc (`:64-66`) and the inline comments (`:360-363`, `:373-375`) describe the view-only case as a complexity that is not editable term data, and so does `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorWindow.fs:12-19`. (5) Test readers follow: `MaterialComplexityTests.fs` `AC-B7 every re-expressed built-in's toProperties reproduces the original preset at reference wavelengths`; `MaterialImportTests.fs` `assertEditableDispersive`, `formula 2 segment carries the page's wavelength_range in µm` and the facts S1.1 steps 1 and 2 added, which now match the record itself; `LibraryFacetsTests.fs` `anisotropyOf reads the re-seeded coded presets from data`; and `OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs` `a coded-preset material (spectrum-spanning band) never flags`, which drops its option match and its comment's former-`None` clause. In `MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs`, `ofComplexity round-trips the editable built-ins value-identically through toComplexity`, `init seeds a new material, an existing editable entry, and a view-only entry` and the two Save facts read the value. (6) Two facts lose their subject and are deleted. `every built-in carries Some complexity after the step-004 re-seed` (`MaterialComplexityTests.fs:132-148`) is now guaranteed by the type. `spec 0040 006: a coded preset with no stored tree still renders all components` (`MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs:1053-1064`) needs an entry without a complexity, which no longer exists; the view-only class restriction stays covered by `spec 0040 006: a view-only entry reads the class off its stored complexity tree — Langasite carries g₁₁ / g₃₃`. Three facts are renamed because their names state the option: `Save adds a NEW material with complexity Some, updates an EXISTING one, and Cancel writes nothing` becomes `Save adds a NEW material with its complexity, updates an EXISTING one, and Cancel writes nothing`; `acceptance: Save round-trips a NEW entry through MaterialProxy with complexity Some` becomes `acceptance: Save round-trips a NEW entry through MaterialProxy with its complexity`; and `a complexity-less entry opens view-only with no Save affordance and no ladder` becomes `a non-editable entry opens view-only with no Save affordance and no ladder`. (7) In every file this step edits, each comment and failure message that says `complexity = None`, `complexity = Some` or `Some complexity` is rewritten or deleted.", "acceptance": "After `complexity` becomes mandatory, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, one fact fewer for the deleted MaterialComplexityTests fact; ui-tests (MaterialEditorWindowTests, MaterialsWindowTests, NkDispersionChartTests, OutOfBandBadgeTests, FsxAcceptanceTests) MUST pass, one fact fewer for the deleted coded-preset fact and with the renamed Save fact; ui-smoke MUST pass with the two renamed facts; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialStore.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryFacets.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OutOfBandDiagnostic.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/MaterialComplexityEditor.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/MaterialImport.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/NkDispersionChart.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialEditorWindow.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryFacetsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialImportTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OutOfBandDiagnosticTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SampleProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "delete", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialComplexityTests.every built-in carries Some complexity after the step-004 re-seed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialComplexityTests.fs", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"op": "delete", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.spec 0040 006: a coded preset with no stored tree still renders all components", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.Save adds a NEW material with complexity Some, updates an EXISTING one, and Cancel writes nothing", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.Save adds a NEW material with its complexity, updates an EXISTING one, and Cancel writes nothing", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.acceptance: Save round-trips a NEW entry through MaterialProxy with complexity Some", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.acceptance: Save round-trips a NEW entry through MaterialProxy with its complexity", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"op": "rename", "suite": "ui-smoke", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.a complexity-less entry opens view-only with no Save affordance and no ladder", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-smoke", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.a non-editable entry opens view-only with no Save affordance and no ladder", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests.init seeds a new material, an existing editable entry, and a view-only entry", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialEditorWindowTests.fs", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}], "contracts": [{"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Domain.MaterialLibrary.MaterialEntry.complexity", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialEditorView.EditorMode", "op": "change_shape", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}, {"symbol": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.NkDispersionChart.previewAnisotropy", "op": "retire", "obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"], "preserves_obligations": ["S12-MANDATORY"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.2 -- A material's physics is its complexity"}
{"number": 14, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.2e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [13], "how_to": "The last mentions of the optional complexity go, so `git grep -n -E \"complexity = (None|Some)\" -- Berreman/` finds nothing; from S1.3's first step its invariant `s03-complexity-mandatory` runs that grep after every step. No code changes. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs:459` and `:480`: the comments say Silicon is view-only because its complexity is not editable term data. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs`: `siliconEntry`'s doc (`:27`) says Silicon's dispersion is the published silicon law. `spec 0040 006: the gyration builder draws all six components for a coded preset with no stored class` (`:194-200`) is renamed `spec 0040 006: the gyration builder draws all six components when every component is requested`, and its comment no longer names a coded preset; its assertions are unchanged. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj:120-124`: the existing comment ends at 'Save round-trips through MaterialProxy'. No comment is added.", "acceptance": "After the sweep, ui-tests MUST pass over every class the test project compiles, because the step edits its project file, with the renamed NkDispersionChartTests fact; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the four s02 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppShellSeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CatalogueTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartFontTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartStyleTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMovementTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRendererBindingTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FacetedTreeControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LocalizationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RayPositionControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererTestTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RotationControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleLibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToBeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToReflectedTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SourceAndDetectorMoveTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TestLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MaterialsWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "rename", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests.spec 0040 006: the gyration builder draws all six components for a coded preset with no stored class", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/NkDispersionChartTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "discovery_gate": "ui-tests", "successor": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests.spec 0040 006: the gyration builder draws all six components when every component is requested", "obligations": ["S12-SWEEP"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.2 -- A material's physics is its complexity"}
{"number": 15, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.3a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [], "how_to": "One place names each built-in identity (.spec-md §3.3; 001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash'). This step moves the identity literals into two well-known id modules and deletes the Ui's `SeedEntryIds`. The preset ids keep their current text until step 20 mints their GUIDs, so every value and every fact is unchanged here. `SeedEntryIds` goes in the same step that adds `PresetIds`, because their shared names (`source600`, `detectorIntensity`, `polarizerLp`, `polarizerCpLeft`, `polarizerCpRight`) may not coexist (ELEV015). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`, module `Library`, directly after `newSampleId` (`:47`): add `module SampleIds` and `module PresetIds`, plain modules shaped like `MaterialLibrary.MaterialIds` (`MaterialLibrary.fs:50-62`): no `[<RequireQualifiedAccess>]`, no `[<Literal>]`, every member a typed value. They sit here and not in `MaterialLibrary.fs` because `SampleId` is declared at `:36` and this file compiles after `MaterialLibrary.fs`; `MaterialIds` and `CategoryIds` stay where they are. (a) `SampleIds` holds eleven `SampleId` values whose literals MOVE out of `SeedSamples` (each `id = Guid.Parse \"…\" |> SampleId` at `:655`, `:665`, `:675`, `:685`, `:695`, `:705`, `:732`, `:758`, `:768`, `:778`, `:788`): `glassPlate1mmId`, `glassPlate2mmId`, `glassFilm600Id`, `glassVacuumId`, `glassFilm200Id`, `multilayerQwId`, `euvMoSiId`, `uniaxialId`, `biaxialId`, `activeCrystalPlateId` and `langasiteSiliconId`. The `Id` suffix keeps each public name unique beside the same-named `SeedSamples` value (ELEV015), which S1.7 deletes. Each `SeedSamples` record reads its member (`id = SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId`). (b) `PresetIds` holds 33 `ElementValueId` values, one per seeded preset, each written `ElementValueId \"<its current id>\"`: `source600` src-600; the `lasers` (`:832-846`) `heNe633` src-hene-633, `heNe543` src-hene-543, `argon488` src-ar-488, `argon515` src-ar-515, `heCd442` src-hecd-442, `heCd325` src-hecd-325, `diode405` src-diode-405, `ruby694` src-ruby-694, `tiSapphire800` src-tisa-800, `ndYag1064` src-ndyag-1064, `ndYag532` src-ndyag-532, `ndYag355` src-ndyag-355, `ndYag266` src-ndyag-266, `erbium1550` src-er-1550, `co2Laser10600` src-co2-10600; the `lithography` sources (`:853-860`) `mercuryG436` src-hg-g-436, `mercuryH405` src-hg-h-405, `mercuryI365` src-hg-i-365, `krf248` src-krf-248, `arf193` src-arf-193, `f2Excimer157` src-f2-157, `euv13p5` src-euv-13p5, `beuv6p7` src-beuv-6p7; the `tunables` (`:867-870`) `xenonMonochromator` src-xe-mono, `tiSapphireTunable` src-tisa-tunable, `supercontinuum` src-supercontinuum, `euvBeamline` src-euv-beamline; and (`:887-891`) `detectorIntensity` det-intensity, `detectorEllipsometer` det-ellipsometer, `polarizerLp` pol-lp, `polarizerCpLeft` pol-cp-left and `polarizerCpRight` pol-cp-right. `SeedSources` passes the members to `source` and `tunable` (`:827-870`); `seedEntries`' five detector and polarizer records (`:887-891`) and `seedTrees`' five detector and polarizer leaves (`:954-962`) read them, so each id is written once. (c) Docs, one to three lines each: `PresetIds` is the frozen identity of every seeded light-source, detector and polarizer preset, the one place a built-in preset's entry id is written (spec 0050 §3.3); `SampleIds` is the frozen identity of every seeded sample. `SampleId`'s doc (`:31-35`) and the `SeedSamples` doc (`:646-650`) say the fixed literals live in `SampleIds`. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs`, `detectorKindOf`'s doc (`:23-27`): the intensity and ellipsometer presets are named `PresetIds.detectorIntensity` / `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer`, not by their id text. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `module SeedEntryIds` and its doc (`:985-1000`) are deleted. `CatalogueKind.defaultSeedEntry` (`:1009-1014`) returns `Some Library.PresetIds.source600`, `detectorIntensity`, `polarizerLp` and `polarizerCpLeft`, and its doc's `pol-cp-right` (`:1008`) reads `PresetIds.polarizerCpRight`. `paletteButtons`' CPL and CPR prebinds (`:2052-2053`) are `Some Library.PresetIds.polarizerCpLeft` and `Some Library.PresetIds.polarizerCpRight`. (4) The four test files that named `SeedEntryIds` read `PresetIds`, and every other seeded preset id in them switches too, comments included. A fixture holds a preset or sample id as an `ElementValueId`, and a helper that wrapped a `string` id takes the `ElementValueId`, so no fixture re-wraps `.value` (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin', which holds for fixtures). (a) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainSceneMsgTests.fs`: the theory `AddElement lands PRE-BOUND to the kind's seeded default entry` (`:108-121`) cannot take a member through `InlineData`, so its rows carry the kind code only (\"S\", \"D\", \"LP\", \"CP\") and a private `expectedSeedOf (code : string) : ElementValueId` maps each code to its member; its name, its four rows and its assertions are unchanged. `AddElementBoundTo carries an explicit pre-bind — the CPR palette button's path` (`:135-140`), the palette fact (`:151-153`) and the detector binds (`:479-496`, `:587-593`) read the members. (b) `TableAndElementRotationTests.fs:532`: the expected prebinds are `Some PresetIds.polarizerLp`, `Some PresetIds.polarizerCpLeft` and `Some PresetIds.polarizerCpRight`. (c) `ExperimentControlsTests.fs`: `bind` (`:31-32`) takes `entryId : ElementValueId`; `glassFilm200Id`, `glassFilm600Id`, `glassPlate1mmId` and `euvMirrorId` (`:40-47`) hold the sample's `entryId` itself, and `BindValueId (ElementValueId glassFilm200Id)` (`:631`) passes `glassFilm200Id`. `withTunableSource` (`:36`) binds `PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`, `:109` binds `PresetIds.heNe633` and `:280` binds `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer`; `:308` and `:347` read the members, and the comments at `:307`, `:308` and `:318` name them. (d) `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs`: `TableRun.sourceEntry` becomes an `ElementValueId`; `tableRun`'s `source` parameter follows, and `userSource` returns the `ElementValueId` it saves. `runOnTable` binds `run.sourceEntry` and `PresetIds.detectorIntensity` directly; `glassOnTable` and the two 600 nm runs pass `PresetIds.source600`; `xenon` is `PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`; `euvAgainstWaveLength` passes `PresetIds.euvBeamline`. Its test-local user source \"src-test-10nm\" stays.", "acceptance": "After the identities move, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke and ui-tests over the selected classes MUST pass with unchanged counts and every fact holding its assertion, the theory `AddElement lands PRE-BOUND to the kind's seeded default entry` keeping its four rows; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ExperimentDataLoad.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/MainSceneMsgTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/TableAndElementRotationTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ExperimentControlsTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.3 -- Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID"}
{"number": 16, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.3b", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [15], "how_to": "The constructor suite names every seeded preset through `PresetIds` (.spec-md §3.3) while the ids still hold their step-15 text, so every fact keeps its meaning and its result. Every occurrence in the files below, comments included, switches. Afterwards `git grep -n -E \"(src|det|pol)-[a-z0-9]\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests` lists only ids that are not seeded presets, and they stay: the test-local user sources of `SourceLibraryTests.fs` (\"src-user-1\", \"src-a\", \"src-b\", \"src-c\", \"src-user-krf\"), the tunable fixture \"src-t\" (`ExperimentRunTests.fs:79`), and the `SourceSpecId`s of `EnvironmentRoundTripTests.fs:64` and `:106` and `SourceProjectionTests.fs:25`, which name spectral source specs (`SourceSpec.fs:243`), not Library presets. A fixture holds an id as an `ElementValueId` (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin'). (1) `ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.fs:46-48`, `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs:56-60` and `:76-79`, and `ExperimentProxyTests.fs:38-39`, `:197-219`, `:238`, `:338` and `:365`: each `BoundByEntryId (ElementValueId \"…\")` is `BoundByEntryId PresetIds.source600`, `BoundByEntryId PresetIds.polarizerLp` or `BoundByEntryId PresetIds.detectorIntensity`. (2) `LibraryProxyTests.fs`, `tryGetEntry hits a known id and misses an unknown id` (`:63-69`): it looks up `PresetIds.source600` and asserts `Assert.Equal(PresetIds.source600, s.id)`; the unknown id \"no-such-id\" stays. (3) `PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs`: `entry` (`:25-28`) and `bind` (`:67-68`) take an `ElementValueId`; `mirrorId`, `thinFilmId` and `plateId` (`:31-35`) hold the sample's `entryId`, and `sourceId` (`:37`) is `PresetIds.source600`. (4) `PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs`: the expected protected ids (`:140-143`) are the `.value` of the five detector and polarizer members plus the seeded sources' ids, sorted as today. `polarizer` (`:147-152`) and `extractedLabels` (`:173-177`) take an `ElementValueId` and compare ids, and their callers (`:153-158`, `:178-180`) pass the members. (5) `SceneProxyTests.fs:32` and `SceneRoundTripTests.fs:32`, `:38` and `:105`: `Some PresetIds.source600` and `Some PresetIds.polarizerLp`. (6) `SourceLibraryTests.fs`: `wavelengthOf` (`:38`) takes an `ElementValueId`, and its seven checks (`:39-45`) read `PresetIds.source600`, `heNe633`, `ndYag1064`, `mercuryI365`, `krf248`, `arf193` and `euv13p5`; the live-Library fact's detector (`:114`) is `PresetIds.detectorIntensity`, in its record and in the lookup.", "acceptance": "After the switch, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass with an unchanged count, every fact of ExperimentCollectionProxyTests, ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests, ExperimentProxyTests, LibraryProxyTests, PlacedSampleEmissionTests, PolarizerBehaviorTests, SceneProxyTests, SceneRoundTripTests and SourceLibraryTests holding its assertion; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/ExperimentProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/PolarizerBehaviorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneProxyTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SceneRoundTripTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.3 -- Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID"}
{"number": 17, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.3c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [15], "how_to": "`OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs` names every seeded preset through `PresetIds` (.spec-md §3.3) while the ids still hold their step-15 text, so every fact keeps its result. Every occurrence, comments included, switches; afterwards `git grep -n -E \"(src|det|pol)-[a-z0-9]\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs` finds nothing. (1) Each `ElementValueId \"src-600\"`, `\"pol-lp\"`, `\"pol-cp-left\"`, `\"det-intensity\"` and `\"det-ellipsometer\"` is its member, inside `ConstructorUiId.libraryEntryNode`, `.libraryEntryCode`, `SelectLibraryEntry` and `SelectLibraryEntryNode` as well. (2) Text compared with `filteredEntryIds` (`:227-228`) or with the `onSelected` recorder (`:214`) is built from the member: `PresetIds.source600.value` (`:437`, `:623`), `PresetIds.polarizerLp.value` (`:447`), `[ PresetIds.polarizerLp.value ]` (`:1080`), and `\"selected:\" + PresetIds.detectorIntensity.value` (`:1102`, `:1106`) or `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer.value` (`:1151`). The two lists the facts sort (`:1072-1074`, `:1143-1145`) are written `List.sort [ PresetIds.polarizerCpLeft.value; PresetIds.polarizerCpRight.value ]` and `List.sort [ PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer.value; PresetIds.detectorIntensity.value ]`, so they hold whatever the ids spell. (3) The id-format facts build their expected text from the member: `\"FacetTreeNode_entry:\" + PresetIds.source600.value` (`:251`) and `\"branch:\" + entryKindFacetKey.value + \":Source:entry:\" + PresetIds.source600.value` (`:369-371`). (4) The Select-bay rows (`:1372`, `:1383`) are `ConstructorUiId.libraryEntry PresetIds.detectorIntensity.uiKey`, the key the bay gives its leaf rows (`ElementValueId.uiKey`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:28`).", "acceptance": "After the switch, ui-tests (LibraryWindowTests) and ui-smoke MUST pass with unchanged counts, every fact holding its assertion; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.3 -- Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID"}
{"number": 18, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.3d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [15], "how_to": "The rest of the UI suite names every seeded preset through `PresetIds` (.spec-md §3.3) while the ids still hold their step-15 text. Every occurrence in the files below, comments included, switches. Afterwards `git grep -n -E \"(src|det|pol)-[a-z0-9]\" -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests` lists only test-local ids, which stay: the user sources \"src-new-1\", \"src-x\", \"src-y\", \"src-u\", \"src-mine\" and \"src-typed\" of `LightSourceEditorTests.fs`, \"src-x\" of `ScrollExtentTests.fs:149`, \"src-test-10nm\" of `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs` and \"src-tune\" of `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs:289-292`. A fixture holds an id as an `ElementValueId`, and a helper that wrapped a `string` id takes the `ElementValueId` (AGENTS.md 'Elevate at origin'). (1) `ElementRendererBindingTests.fs`: `drawableOf` (`:26-27`) takes `valueId : ElementValueId option`; `stateOf` (`:63-64`) follows, wrapping its test-local ids where it writes them (`Some (ElementValueId \"lib:sample\")`); the HideNormals fact (`:92`) draws `Some PresetIds.polarizerLp`. (2) `InverseConstructorTests.fs:155`: `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer`. (3) `LightSourceEditorTests.fs:173`: `PresetIds.euv13p5`; `:210`: `PresetIds.arf193`. (4) `SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs`: `baseExperiment` (`:61`) takes `srcBind : ElementValueId option` and `detBind : ElementValueId option`, `bindOne` binds the id it receives, and every call (`:134-259`) passes `Some PresetIds.source600` with `Some PresetIds.detectorIntensity`, or `Some PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer` at `:182`. (5) `WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs:253-261` and `WireUiCompositionTests.fs:197`: `ConstructorUiId.libraryEntryNode PresetIds.source600`, `PresetIds.polarizerLp` and `PresetIds.polarizerCpLeft`. (6) `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs`: `bind` (`:40`) and `filmOnR2` (`:158`) take an `ElementValueId`; `glassFilm200Id` and `glassPlate1mmId` (`:41-42`) hold the sample's `entryId`; the binds and lookups read `PresetIds.heNe633` (`:68`, `:123-125`, `:176`, `:185`), `arf193` (`:79`), `krf248` (`:137`, `:150`), `xenonMonochromator` (`:167`, `:184`), `source600` (`:190`, `:254`), `detectorEllipsometer` (`:202`) and `detectorIntensity` (`:129`).", "acceptance": "After the switch, ui-tests (ElementRendererBindingTests, InverseConstructorTests, LightSourceEditorTests, SolverHandoffWindowTests, WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests) and ui-smoke, which holds WireUi0040CompositionTests and WireUiCompositionTests, MUST pass with unchanged counts, every fact holding its assertion; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRendererBindingTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ElementRendererBindingTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUi0040CompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WireUiCompositionTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.3 -- Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID"}
{"number": 19, "anchor": "ADD_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.3e", "red": "RED_0004", "expected_red": ["constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests"], "red_in": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests"], "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests"], "depends_on": [16, 18], "how_to": "Red first for 001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash' (.spec-md §3.3): every seeded entry id, and every minted source id, is the canonical string of a GUID. Facts only; no production file changes. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs`, beside the seeded-sources facts: (a) `every seeded Library entry id is the canonical string of a GUID, and no two are equal`: for every entry of `seedEntries`, `Guid.TryParse e.entryId.value` succeeds (matched, never `.IsSome`) and the parsed GUID's `string` equals `e.entryId.value`, the lowercase hyphenated form `SampleId.toElementValueId` writes (`ElementId.fs:43`); and the ids are distinct. The samples pass; it fails today on the presets' text ids. (b) `newSourceId mints the canonical string of a fresh GUID`: two `newSourceId ()` calls each parse as a GUID whose `string` equals the id, and the two differ. It fails today on the `src-` prefix (`ElementId.fs:594`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs`, `Add source opens the editor on a freshly minted source id` (`:144-149`): its name and its first two assertions stay; `Assert.StartsWith(\"source-add:src-\", calls.[0])` becomes: `calls.[0]` starts with `source-add:` and the rest is the canonical string of a GUID. It fails today.", "acceptance": "After the facts land, constructor-unit-tests (SourceLibraryTests) MUST fail with exactly `every seeded Library entry id is the canonical string of a GUID, and no two are equal` and `newSourceId mints the canonical string of a fresh GUID`, every other SourceLibraryTests fact passing; ui-tests (LightSourceEditorTests) MUST fail with exactly `Add source opens the editor on a freshly minted source id`, every other LightSourceEditorTests fact passing; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests"]}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests.every seeded Library entry id is the canonical string of a GUID, and no two are equal", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S13-GUID-IDS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests.newSourceId mints the canonical string of a fresh GUID", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S13-GUID-IDS"]}, {"op": "change_expectation", "suite": "ui-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests.Add source opens the editor on a freshly minted source id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs", "obligations": ["S13-GUID-IDS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.3 -- Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID"}
{"number": 20, "anchor": "CLOSE_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.3e", "closes": "RED_0004", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [19], "how_to": "Every seeded preset gets its frozen GUID, and a new user source is a plain GUID (.spec-md §3.3; 001 §B). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs`, `PresetIds`: the text of each of the 33 members becomes a GUID minted once while implementing (`[guid]::NewGuid()`), written `ElementValueId \"<guid>\"` in the lowercase hyphenated form a `Guid`'s `string` prints. No two are equal, and none equals a `MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds` or `SampleIds` literal. From this step the literals are frozen: S1.5 exports them byte-for-byte. (2) `newSourceId` (`:592-594`) mints `ElementValueId (string (Guid.NewGuid ()))`; its doc says the id is a plain GUID string, as a sample's is (`SampleId.toElementValueId`, `:43`). (3) `LibraryEntry.entryId`'s doc (`:355-356`) says every entry id is the string of a GUID: a sample's `SampleId`, a preset's `PresetIds` member, a user source's minted id. `liveLibrary` (`:1130-1168`) keeps its code: its `Guid.TryParse` probe (`:1159`) now parses a preset id too, finds no sample (`SampleStore.fs:119` answers `Ok None` for an unknown id) and falls through to the presets. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs` gains `the live Library resolves a seeded preset, a user source and a sample by their GUID ids`: over `liveLibrary (createInMemory ()) samples sources`, with a user source saved under `newSourceId ()` and a sample saved under `newSampleId ()`, `tryGetEntry` returns the ellipsometer detector for `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer`, the user source for its id and the sample for `toElementValueId` of its id, and `Ok None` for a fresh GUID that names nothing. (5) No product ordering changes. A fact that fails only because it relied on the old ids' alphabetical order compares order-independently, with its assertion otherwise unchanged. Afterwards `git grep -n -E \"(src-(600|hene-|ar-4|ar-5|hecd-|diode-|ruby-|tisa-|ndyag-|er-1550|co2-|hg-|krf-|arf-|f2-1|euv-|beuv-|xe-mono|supercontinuum)|det-(intensity|ellipsometer)|pol-(lp|cp-left|cp-right))\" -- \"Berreman/*.fs\"` finds nothing; from S1.4's first step its invariant `s04-no-seeded-string-preset-ids` runs that grep after every step.", "acceptance": "After the GUIDs are minted, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every seeded Library entry id is the canonical string of a GUID, and no two are equal` and `newSourceId mints the canonical string of a fresh GUID`, which step 19 left red, and `the live Library resolves a seeded preset, a user source and a sample by their GUID ids`; ui-tests over the selected classes MUST pass, including `Add source opens the editor on a freshly minted source id`; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the five s03 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-tests", "ui-smoke"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppShellSeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CatalogueTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.CategoryEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartFontTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ChartStyleTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMenuTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementMovementTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRendererBindingTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ExperimentControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FacetedTreeControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LayerBandsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LocalizationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainSceneMsgTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MainWorkbenchTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.NkDispersionChartTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RayPositionControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RendererTestTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.RotationControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleLibraryControlsTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToBeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SnapToReflectedTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SourceAndDetectorMoveTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableAndElementRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TableRotationTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.TestLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WireUiFinalCompositionTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests"]}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/ElementId.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests.the live Library resolves a seeded preset, a user source and a sample by their GUID ids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/SourceLibraryTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.SourceLibraryTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S13-GUID-IDS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.3 -- Every library entry is identified by a frozen GUID"}
{"number": 21, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4a", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Ui", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [20], "how_to": "One serializer options value, owned by a new canonical-JSON module (001 §B: the System.Text.Json + FSharp.SystemTextJson + JsonSchema.Net stack in `ProjectJson` is REUSED; .spec-md §5 'Canonical JSON + SHA-256', §6 'JSON + schema'). This step is a MOVE and changes no output. (1) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs`, `module CanonicalJson` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Storage`, compiled directly after `SchemaValidation.fs` and before `ProjectJson.fs` (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:22-23`): one `<Compile Include=\"CanonicalJson.fs\" />` line and no new comment. `ProjectJson.options` (`ProjectJson.fs:125-145`) and its five private converters (`BeamBranchConverter`, `RotationLockConverter`, `BeamPresenceConverter`, `ToggleStateConverter`, `ComplexMatrixConverter`, `ProjectJson.fs:24-123`) MOVE there verbatim. Their docs say that this is the one options value every JSON store of the app reads. They are deleted from `ProjectJson.fs`, whose `parseProject` and `serializeProject` (`:158-182`) now read `CanonicalJson.options`; any `open` that is no longer used goes. (2) Every other reader re-points, with no other change: `GroupsLibrary.fs` (`:82`, `:90`, `:93`), `RecentFiles.fs` (`:55`, `:70`), the three reads in `Report.fs` module `MaterialLibrary` (`importMaterials` / `exportMaterials`), `OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs` (`:367`, `:377`, `:380`) and `OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs` (`AC-D8 only dndT and referenceTemperature persist through JSON (operating T unstored)`). The inventory's census of `ProjectJson.options` is exactly these files and `ProjectJson.fs`. (3) Every comment that names the moved value or one of its converters names `CanonicalJson` instead: `GroupsLibrary.fs:17` and `:86`, `RecentFiles.fs:12`, the two `Report.fs` docs that name the shared options, `UserEnvironment.fs:13`, `:141`, `:250` and `:373`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui/Localization.fs:39`, `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Groups.fs:16`, `:23` and `:123`, and `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Placement.fs:279`. No other comment is swept. Afterwards `git grep -n -F \"ProjectJson.options\" -- Berreman/` finds nothing. No converter is added and no option changes, so every existing JSON round-trip fact (`ProjectJsonRoundtripTests`, `RoundTripTests`, `GroupsRoundTripTests`, `EnvironmentRoundTripTests`, `ExportImportTests`, `DispersionModelsTests`) passes unchanged.", "acceptance": "After the move, `CanonicalJson.options` MUST be the only serializer options value, with nothing under Berreman/ naming `ProjectJson.options`, and every existing JSON round-trip fact MUST pass unchanged; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, the selected ui-tests classes and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppShellSeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LocalizationTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/ProjectJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/GroupsLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/RecentFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Report.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/Localization.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Groups.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/Placement.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/DispersionModelsTests.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 22, "anchor": "ADD_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.4b", "red": "RED_0005", "expected_red": ["constructor-unit-tests"], "red_in": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests"], "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [21], "how_to": "Red first: two kinds of number that the shared options cannot carry and that entry files hold (001 §B: 'Any entry that cannot serialise is a test failure'). Facts only; no production file changes. New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs`: `module CanonicalJsonTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Tests`, appended to `OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj`'s compile list after `PlacedSampleEmissionTests.fs`, with no new comment. It holds three facts over `CanonicalJson.options` (step 21). (1) `a complex number survives the shared options as its real and imaginary parts`: `Complex(1.5, -0.25)` serialized and read back is equal, and its JSON is a two-element number array. It is red today, because System.Text.Json writes `Real`, `Imaginary`, `Magnitude` and `Phase` and reads back zero. (2) `a real matrix survives the shared options as its rows`: the Mueller matrix `Propagation.analyzerMueller IdealLinear` at 30° (built as `PolarizerBehaviorTests` builds `lp0`), serialized and read back, is equal element for element, with bit-identical doubles, and its JSON is four arrays of four numbers. It is red today, because reading `Matrix<double>` throws `NotSupportedException` (an abstract type): only `Matrix<Complex>` has a converter. (3) `an absorbing built-in material survives the shared options`: the complexity of the `builtInEntries` entry `MaterialIds.euvMolybdenum` (an `IsotropicAbsorbing` complex index) serialized and read back is equal. It is red today for the reason of (1). No fact catches an exception: a throw is the failure.", "acceptance": "After the facts land, constructor-unit-tests (CanonicalJsonTests) MUST fail with exactly `a complex number survives the shared options as its real and imaginary parts`, `a real matrix survives the shared options as its rows` and `an absorbing built-in material survives the shared options`, the class's only facts; and build, elevation and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.a complex number survives the shared options as its real and imaginary parts", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-NUMBERS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.a real matrix survives the shared options as its rows", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-NUMBERS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.an absorbing built-in material survives the shared options", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-NUMBERS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 23, "anchor": "CLOSE_RED", "ac": "AC-S1.4b", "closes": "RED_0005", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage"], "depends_on": [22], "how_to": "`CanonicalJson.options` gains two converters (001 §B; .spec-md §5). They sit beside `ComplexMatrixConverter` and are written as it is: private `JsonConverter` classes, registered before the `JsonFSharpConverter`. (1) `ComplexConverter` writes a `System.Numerics.Complex` as `[re, im]` and reads that pair back. (2) `RealMatrixConverter` writes a MathNet `Matrix<double>` as an array of rows and reads it back through `Matrix<double>.Build.DenseOfArray`, as `ComplexMatrixConverter` (moved from `ProjectJson.fs:92-123` in step 21) reads its cells. A malformed value throws `JsonException` inside the converter, and the callers already map that to `MalformedJsonErr` (as `ProjectJson.fs` `ProjectJsonText.parseProject` does). The options' doc names the two. No other option changes. The project, groups and environment formats gain the same form for a complex scalar. No schema constrains it (the `$defs` of `schema/optical-constructor-project.schema.json` hold no complex object), so their facts stay green.", "acceptance": "After the converters are added, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a complex number survives the shared options as its real and imaginary parts`, `a real matrix survives the shared options as its rows` and `an absorbing built-in material survives the shared options`, which step 22 left red; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 24, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4c", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [20], "how_to": "The identities, the provenance and the name rule of the library-entry files, in Domain (001 §A; 001 §B 'Every entry file carries'; .spec-md §3.11, §5). New `OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: `module LibraryEntryFiles` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Domain`, compiled directly after `ElementId.fs` (one `<Compile>` line right after `ElementId.fs`'s in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj`) and with no new comment. It opens `MaterialLibrary`, `Library`, `Placement` and `Softellect.Sys.Primitives` (`FileName`, `FileExtension`). Every type follows `AGENTS.md`: single-case unions carry `.value`, case names have two words, no `bool` appears, and each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050. (1) `LibraryEntryKind`: `MaterialEntryKind`, `SampleEntryKind`, `SourceEntryKind`, `PolarizerEntryKind`, `DetectorEntryKind` and `CategoryEntryKind` (S7.1 adds the item-model kind). `member value : int` answers 1 to 6 in that order, and `static member tryOfWire (v : int) : LibraryEntryKind option` answers `None` for any other tag. `member extension : FileExtension` answers `.material-json`, `.sample-json`, `.source-json`, `.polarizer-json`, `.detector-json` and `.category-json` (001 §A). `member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` answers 1 for every kind. `static member all : LibraryEntryKind list` lists the six in tag order. (2) `FileSchemaVersion of int` is the schema version a stored file declares, and `EntrySchema = { kind : LibraryEntryKind; version : FileSchemaVersion }`. (3) `LibraryEntryId of Guid` is an entry's frozen GUID, whatever its kind (001 §B 'Identity is GUID + version + hash'). Type extensions after it: `MaterialId.toLibraryEntryId`, `SampleId.toLibraryEntryId` and `CategoryId.toLibraryEntryId` keep the GUID. `ElementValueId.tryToLibraryEntryId : LibraryEntryId option` parses a preset's id and answers `None` for any other text; since step 20, every seeded and minted preset id is the canonical string of a GUID. No conversion goes the other way (ELEV006): step 25's decoders build a kind's id at the file seam. (4) `CatalogueId of Guid`, `CatalogueName of string` and `KitId of Guid`. `KitId` is the GUID a kit's `.kit-json` carries (001 §E). The provenance needs it now, so it is born here, and S4.1's `Kit` module MUST reuse this type rather than declare a second one (ELEV014). (5) Provenance (001 §B): `MaterialSourceName`, `MaterialSourceRecordId`, `MaterialSourceVersion`, `EntryLicence` (an SPDX identifier, e.g. `CC0-1.0` or `CC-BY-4.0`) and `EntryCitation`, each `of string`; `SourcePullInfo = { source : MaterialSourceName; record : MaterialSourceRecordId; sourceVersion : MaterialSourceVersion; licence : EntryLicence; citation : EntryCitation }`; and `EntryProvenance` = `BuiltInProvenance of CatalogueId` | `UserProvenance` | `KitImportProvenance of KitId` | `SourcePullProvenance of SourcePullInfo`. A built-in's protection derives from its provenance: `member protection : EntryProtection` answers `ProtectedBuiltIn` for `BuiltInProvenance` and `UserManaged` for the rest, and `member categoryOrigin : CategoryOrigin` answers `BuiltInCategory` or `UserCategory` by the same rule. (6) `ContentHash of string` is the lowercase hex SHA-256 of an entry's canonical content. Storage computes it (step 27). (7) The name rule (001 §A; .spec-md §3.11) is `FileStem of string`. `static member ofText (text : string) : FileStem` replaces each of `: * ? \" < > |` and the separators `/` and `\\` with `_` and keeps every other character. `member withExtension (extension : FileExtension) : FileName` answers the stem followed by the extension. `EntryName.fileStem : FileStem` is a type extension. No reserved-name, length or trimming rule is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs` (`module LibraryEntryFilesTests`), appended to the compile list after `CanonicalJsonTests.fs`. (a) `every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension`: the six tags in order, `tryOfWire` inverse to `value`, `None` for 0 and 7, the six extensions exactly as above, version 1 and `all` in tag order. (b) `a file stem keeps the name's characters and replaces only the ones Windows forbids`: `Ti:sapphire laser, tunable 700–1000 nm` becomes `Ti_sapphire laser, tunable 700–1000 nm`; `a/b\\c*d?e\"f<g>h|i:j` becomes `a_b_c_d_e_f_g_h_i_j`; `Langasite (La3Ga5SiO14)` and `CO₂ laser 10.6 µm` are unchanged; and `(EntryName \"Silicon\").fileStem.withExtension MaterialEntryKind.extension` is `FileName \"Silicon.material-json\"`. (c) `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed`: `protection` and `categoryOrigin` of each of the four provenance cases. (d) `a library entry id keeps the GUID of the kind's own id`: `MaterialIds.silicon`, `SampleIds.multilayerQwId` and `CategoryIds.glass` keep their GUIDs; `PresetIds.detectorEllipsometer.tryToLibraryEntryId` is the GUID its text spells; and a test-local non-GUID `ElementValueId` answers `None`.", "acceptance": "After `LibraryEntryFiles.fs` lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension`, `a file stem keeps the name's characters and replaces only the ones Windows forbids`, `a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed` and `a library entry id keeps the GUID of the kind's own id`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.every library entry kind round-trips its wire tag and renders its 001 extension", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-IDENTITY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a file stem keeps the name's characters and replaces only the ones Windows forbids", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-IDENTITY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a built-in provenance is protected and every other provenance is user-managed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-IDENTITY"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a library entry id keeps the GUID of the kind's own id", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-IDENTITY"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 25, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4d", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [24], "how_to": "The entry content, its payload and the envelope, with the builders and decoders that join them to the domain values (001 §B; .spec-md §5). In `LibraryEntryFiles.fs`, after step 24's types: (1) The payload holds what the envelope does not, because an entry's id, name, category and description belong to the envelope: `SamplePayloadData = { structure : SampleStructure; substrate : SubstrateKind; supportedEmission : Emission }`, `SourcePayloadData = { waveLength : WaveLength; tuning : SourceTuning }`, `PolarizerPayloadData = { behavior : PolarizerBehavior; category : PolarizerCategory }`, and `LibraryEntryPayload` = `MaterialPayload of MaterialComplexity` | `SamplePayload of SamplePayloadData` | `SourcePayload of SourcePayloadData` | `PolarizerPayload of PolarizerPayloadData` | `DetectorPayload of DetectorKind` | `CategoryPayload of CategoryVisibility`, with `member kind : LibraryEntryKind`. A preset's `protection` and a category's `origin` are not stored, because they derive from the provenance (step 24). (2) `LibraryEntryContent = { schema : EntrySchema; id : LibraryEntryId; version : VersionNumber; name : EntryName; categoryOpt : CategoryId option; descriptionOpt : EntryDescription option; payload : LibraryEntryPayload; provenance : EntryProvenance }` is the entry file without its hash. Its `member fileName : FileName` is `this.name.fileStem.withExtension this.schema.kind.extension`. `categoryOpt` holds a material's category and is `None` for every other kind. Facets are derived from the payload (`LibraryFacets`) and never stored. `VersionNumber` is `MaterialLibrary.fs:VersionNumber`, reused. `LibraryEntryEnvelope = { content : LibraryEntryContent; contentHash : ContentHash }`. The hash covers exactly the content, so the record keeps the two apart while the file stays flat: step 30 writes the content's keys and `contentHash` side by side. (3) `LibraryEntryError` is an `*Error` union whose every case is `of reason : string` naming the entry: `EntryKindMismatchErr` (a decoder was given another kind), `EntryIdNotGuidErr` (a preset id that is not a GUID), `ProvenanceMismatchErr` (a preset's protection or a category's origin disagrees with the provenance it is filed under) and `MissingEntryFieldErr` (a material without a category, or a sample without a description). (4) The builders are static members of `LibraryEntryContent`. Each takes `(version : VersionNumber) (provenance : EntryProvenance)` and then the value, and sets `schema = { kind = payload.kind; version = kind.currentSchemaVersion }`. `ofMaterialEntry` and `ofSample` answer the content. `ofSourcePreset`, `ofDetectorPreset`, `ofPolarizerPreset` and `ofMaterialCategory` answer `Result<LibraryEntryContent, LibraryEntryError>`: they refuse an id that is not a GUID, and a protection or origin that disagrees with `provenance.protection` or `provenance.categoryOrigin`. A category is filed under its `CategoryName` as the entry name through `CategoryName.toEntryName`, a type extension declared here, so no builder re-wraps a `.value` (ELEV001). (5) The decoders are members of `LibraryEntryContent`: `toMaterialEntry`, `toSample`, `toSourcePreset`, `toDetectorPreset`, `toPolarizerPreset` and `toMaterialCategory`, each answering `Result<_, LibraryEntryError>`. Each builds the kind's own id from `this.id` (`MaterialId`, `SampleId`, `CategoryId`, or a preset's `ElementValueId` as the GUID's string) and a category's `CategoryName` from the entry name, takes the protection or origin from the provenance, and answers `EntryKindMismatchErr` for another kind's payload. Each decoder is marked `[<Softellect.Sys.ElevationBoundary(nameof Softellect.Sys.StorageBoundary, \"the library-entry file contract (001 §B): the file's kind-neutral entry GUID becomes the kind's own id\")>]`. This is the one place where an entry GUID becomes a kind's id, and it is the file seam, so the boundary licenses the re-wrap that ELEV001 would otherwise report. A builder followed by its decoder answers the value it was given. Tests, in `LibraryEntryFilesTests`: (a) `every kind's builder and decoder are inverse`: one value of each kind (the `builtInEntries` Langasite, `SeedSamples.multilayerQw`, a `SeedSources.tunables` source and the intensity detector under `BuiltInProvenance`, a test-local `ConstantMueller` polarizer under `UserProvenance`, and the `standardCategories` Glass under `BuiltInProvenance`). Each content's `schema` is its payload's kind at version 1, and its decoder answers the value. (b) `a decoder refuses another kind's content`: `toSample` of a material's content answers `EntryKindMismatchErr`. (c) `a preset or category filed under a provenance that disagrees is refused`: a `ProtectedBuiltIn` source under `UserProvenance` and a `UserCategory` under `BuiltInProvenance` answer `ProvenanceMismatchErr`, and a preset whose id is a test-local non-GUID text answers `EntryIdNotGuidErr`. (d) `a material without a category or a sample without a description does not decode`: a material content with `categoryOpt = None` and a sample content with `descriptionOpt = None` answer `MissingEntryFieldErr`. (e) `an entry's file name is its name made safe plus its kind's extension`: the content of a source named `Ti:sapphire laser 800 nm` has the file name `Ti_sapphire laser 800 nm.source-json`, and Langasite's has `Langasite (La3Ga5SiO14).material-json`.", "acceptance": "After the content model lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every kind's builder and decoder are inverse`, `a decoder refuses another kind's content`, `a preset or category filed under a provenance that disagrees is refused`, `a material without a category or a sample without a description does not decode` and `an entry's file name is its name made safe plus its kind's extension`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.every kind's builder and decoder are inverse", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CONTENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a decoder refuses another kind's content", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CONTENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a preset or category filed under a provenance that disagrees is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CONTENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a material without a category or a sample without a description does not decode", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CONTENT"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.an entry's file name is its name made safe plus its kind's extension", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CONTENT"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 26, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4e", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Domain", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [25], "how_to": "The catalogue manifest (001 §A 'Catalogue folder layout': `.catalogue-json` holds the name, the catalogue id, the version and the entry hashes; .spec-md §5). In `LibraryEntryFiles.fs`: (1) `CatalogueManifestRow = { kind : LibraryEntryKind; id : LibraryEntryId; version : VersionNumber; fileName : FileName; contentHash : ContentHash }`, and `LibraryEntryEnvelope.manifestRow : CatalogueManifestRow`, built from `content.schema.kind`, `content.id`, `content.version`, `content.fileName` and `contentHash`. (2) `CatalogueManifest = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; id : CatalogueId; name : CatalogueName; version : VersionNumber; entries : CatalogueManifestRow list }`, with three static members. `currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` is 1. `extension : FileExtension` is `.catalogue-json`, the one place that text is written, and `fileName : FileName` is `(FileStem.ofText \"\").withExtension extension`, because a file that exists once per folder is named by its extension alone (001 §A). `tryCreate (id : CatalogueId) (name : CatalogueName) (version : VersionNumber) (envelopes : LibraryEntryEnvelope list) : Result<CatalogueManifest, LibraryEntryError>` is the pure per-kind uniqueness check that export uses (001 §A). Two envelopes of one kind whose file names are equal ignoring case (the Windows file system's rule, `StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase`) are `DuplicateEntryFileNameErr`, naming both entries. Two envelopes with the same id and version are `DuplicateEntryVersionErr`. Both cases join `LibraryEntryError`. Equal names of different kinds are allowed, because their extensions differ. The rows are sorted by kind tag and then ordinally by file name, so a manifest's text does not depend on the order its entries arrived in. The manifest's own hash is not stored in it: Storage computes it (step 31), and S3's start-up import records it. Tests, in `LibraryEntryFilesTests`, over envelopes whose `contentHash` is a test-local 64-character hex literal (Domain does not hash): (a) `a manifest lists one row per envelope, sorted by kind and file name`: a source, a material and a sample, given in that order, become three rows in kind order, each equal to its envelope's `manifestRow`, and `schemaVersion` is 1. (b) `a manifest refuses two entries of one kind with one file name`: two materials named `Silicon` and `silicon`, and two named `Si:O` and `Si_O`, each answer `DuplicateEntryFileNameErr`, while a material and a sample both named `Glass` are accepted. (c) `a manifest refuses one entry version twice`: two envelopes with one id and one version answer `DuplicateEntryVersionErr`.", "acceptance": "After the manifest model lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a manifest lists one row per envelope, sorted by kind and file name`, `a manifest refuses two entries of one kind with one file name` and `a manifest refuses one entry version twice`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Domain/LibraryEntryFiles.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a manifest lists one row per envelope, sorted by kind and file name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-MANIFEST-MODEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a manifest refuses two entries of one kind with one file name", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-MANIFEST-MODEL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests.a manifest refuses one entry version twice", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.LibraryEntryFilesTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-MANIFEST-MODEL"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 27, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4f", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [23, 24], "how_to": "The canonical form and the content hash (001 §B: `contentHash` is SHA-256 over canonical JSON, with sorted keys and invariant-culture numbers; .spec-md §5). In `CanonicalJson.fs`: (1) `nodeOf<'Value> (value : 'Value) : Result<JsonNode, StorageError>` serializes through `options` into a `JsonNode`. A serializer failure (a non-finite double, an unsupported type) is `MalformedJsonErr` carrying the message, never a throw. (2) The canonical rendering of a `JsonNode` lives in extension members on `JsonNode`, because members may speak primitives while no free function may take or return a bare `string` or `byte[]` (ELEV003). Every object's properties are written in ordinal order of their names (`StringComparer.Ordinal`). Arrays keep their order. Numbers keep the serializer's invariant shortest round-trip text. Strings are escaped by `JavaScriptEncoder.UnsafeRelaxedJsonEscaping`, so names such as `CO₂ laser 10.6 µm` stay readable. No BOM is written. There are two renderings: indented, with two-space indents and `\\n` line ends (`JsonWriterOptions.NewLine`), which is the file form; and compact, with no whitespace, which is the hashed form. (3) `contentHashOf<'Value> (value : 'Value) : Result<ContentHash, StorageError>` is the lowercase hex (`Convert.ToHexStringLower`) SHA-256 (`SHA256.HashData`) of the UTF-8 bytes of the compact canonical rendering of `nodeOf value`. So the hash depends on neither whitespace, key order nor the current culture. Doubles round-trip bit-exactly, because System.Text.Json writes the shortest round-trip text and reads it back with correct IEEE rounding. Tests, in `CanonicalJsonTests`: (a) `canonical text orders every object's keys and ignores the order they came in`: for the node of a test-local tunable `SourcePreset` and a copy with every object's properties reversed recursively, both renderings of the two are equal, and the keys come out in ordinal order. (b) `every double round-trips bit-exactly through canonical text whatever the culture`: the list `0.1; 1.0/3.0; 5e-324; 2.2250738585072014e-308; 1.7976931348623157e308; -0.0; 6.02214076e23; 1e-300` written canonically and read back keeps every value's `BitConverter.DoubleToInt64Bits`, under `CultureInfo(\"de-DE\")` set as the current culture and restored in a `finally`, and the text uses `.` as its decimal point. (c) `the content hash is the lowercase SHA-256 of the compact canonical text`: `contentHashOf` equals the test's own `SHA256.HashData` over the compact rendering's UTF-8, in 64 lowercase hex characters; equal values hash equal, and a changed number hashes differently. (d) `the canonical form of a fixed value is frozen`: for a test-local `MaterialCategory` with a fixed GUID literal and the name `Glass — CO₂ µm`, the indented rendering equals a text literal (LF line ends, two-space indents, the non-ASCII characters unescaped) and `contentHashOf` equals a hash literal. Both literals are the implemented writer's output, captured once while implementing this step and frozen from then on, so any later change to the canonical form fails here before it can change a committed catalogue file's hash (S1.5). (e) `a non-finite number is a typed serialization error`: `nodeOf nan` answers `MalformedJsonErr`.", "acceptance": "After the canonical writer and the hash land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `canonical text orders every object's keys and ignores the order they came in`, `every double round-trips bit-exactly through canonical text whatever the culture`, `the content hash is the lowercase SHA-256 of the compact canonical text`, `the canonical form of a fixed value is frozen` and `a non-finite number is a typed serialization error`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.canonical text orders every object's keys and ignores the order they came in", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CANONICAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.every double round-trips bit-exactly through canonical text whatever the culture", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CANONICAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.the content hash is the lowercase SHA-256 of the compact canonical text", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CANONICAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.the canonical form of a fixed value is frozen", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CANONICAL"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.a non-finite number is a typed serialization error", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CANONICAL"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 28, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4g", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [27], "how_to": "A closed set's disk tag is its int (`AGENTS.md`: 'A closed set's wire/disk tag is an integer'; .spec-md §4 'Shapes'). `CanonicalJson.options` gains four converters, written as step 23's are and registered before the `JsonFSharpConverter`. They cover `LibraryEntryKind` (step 24); S1.1's `TabulatedInterpolation` (step 2) and `PublishedIndexLaw` (step 8); and S1.2's `PublishedGyrationLaw` (step 10). The last three are in `Berreman/Berreman/Dispersion.fs`. Each converter writes the case's `value` and reads through `tryOfWire`. An unknown tag throws `JsonException`, which the callers report as `MalformedJsonErr`. No other union changes its form. The fieldless unions without an int tag (`SubstrateKind`, `DetectorKind`, `CategoryVisibility` and the rest) keep the serializer's case-name form, which the project, groups and environment formats already store. Giving them int tags is out of scope. Tests, in `CanonicalJsonTests`: (a) `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back`: every case of the four sets serializes as its `value` (for example `1`) and reads back equal. (b) `an unknown disk tag is refused`: reading `9` as a `LibraryEntryKind` and `4` as a `PublishedIndexLaw` throws `JsonException`.", "acceptance": "After the tag converters land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back` and `an unknown disk tag is refused`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/CanonicalJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.every closed set with an int tag is written as its tag and read back", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-WIRE-TAGS"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests.an unknown disk tag is refused", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/CanonicalJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.CanonicalJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-WIRE-TAGS"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 29, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4h", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Ui"], "depends_on": [21], "how_to": "`SchemaValidation` is generalised from the one project schema to any build-copied schema (001 §B: 'JSON Schema per kind … REUSED'; .spec-md §6 'JSON + schema'), so one evaluation body serves every format. In `SchemaValidation.fs`, `validateWith (schema : Lazy<Result<JsonSchema, StorageError>>) (element : JsonElement) : Result<unit, StorageError>` holds the evaluation body of today's `validate` (`:64-76`): `EvaluationOptions(OutputFormat = OutputFormat.List)`, `collectMessages` (`:45-59`) and the fallback message `schema validation failed`. `validate` answers `validateWith` over the project schema (`:31-36`), so `ProjectJson` is unchanged. The two copies of that body are deleted and call it: `GroupsLibrary.validateGroupsLibrary` (`GroupsLibrary.fs:49-59`) over its groups schema, and `UserEnvironment.validateUserEnvironment` (`OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs:331-344`) over its environment schema. Both keep their names, their lazies and their `$id`s, and their docs say they reuse `validateWith`. The environment validator's messages now keep their nested instance locations, as the groups validator's already do. `EnvironmentRoundTripTests` asserts only that messages are present, and `GroupsRoundTripTests` that the groups-specific fallback text is absent, so both stay green unchanged. The per-kind schemas arrive with their files in step 30.", "acceptance": "After the generalisation, the project, groups and environment validators MUST share `validateWith`, and `RoundTripTests`, `GroupsRoundTripTests` and `EnvironmentRoundTripTests` MUST pass unchanged; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests, ui-smoke, the selected ui-tests classes and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests", "ui-smoke", "ui-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}, "ui-smoke": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "ui-smoke"}, "ui-tests": {"mode": "selected", "suite": "ui-tests", "values": ["OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppShellSeamTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.DataFilePickerFolderTests", "OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LocalizationTests"]}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/GroupsLibrary.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui/UserEnvironment.fs"], "tests": [], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 30, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4i", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [26, 28, 29], "how_to": "One file per entry: write it, then read it back through schema, version and hash checks (001 §B: 'One entry per file', 'Every entry file carries', 'JSON Schema per kind', 'No up-converters'; .spec-md §5). (1) `Errors.fs`: `StorageError` (`:21-27`) gains `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr of SchemaVersionMismatchInfo` and `ContentHashMismatchErr of ContentHashMismatchInfo`. The two records are declared above it: `SchemaVersionMismatchInfo = { fileExtension : FileExtension; found : FileSchemaVersion; expected : FileSchemaVersion }`, where the extension names the file's kind (001 §A) so that S4's kit files can reuse the case, and `ContentHashMismatchInfo = { entryId : LibraryEntryId; recorded : ContentHash; computed : ContentHash }`. Records carry the two same-typed fields, because a case holding them as a tuple is ELEV011. The doc list (`:11-20`) names both cases. No existing match on `StorageError` is exhaustive, so no consumer changes. (2) Schemas, in draft 2020-12 like `schema/optical-constructor-project.schema.json`, each with its own `$id` (`https://berreman/schema/library-<kind>.json`). `schema/library-common.schema.json` holds, once, the definitions that every entry and the catalogue share: the GUID string, a positive version, the content hash `^[0-9a-f]{64}$` and the four provenance shapes. The others reference it by its `$id`. `schema/library-material.schema.json`, `library-sample`, `library-source`, `library-polarizer`, `library-detector` and `library-category` each describe exactly what this step's writer emits for their kind. Each checks unconditionally that `schema` is `{ kind: <the kind's tag>, version: <a positive integer> }`. Everything else is checked only under `if` `schema.version` is 1 (`then`): every key present and no other (`additionalProperties: false`); `id` a GUID; `name` a non-empty string; `categoryOpt` a GUID for a material and `null` otherwise; `descriptionOpt` a string for a sample, a string or `null` for a material, and `null` otherwise; `payload` the kind's case tag with its record's required keys; `provenance` one of the four shapes; and `contentHash` the hash pattern. The physics inside a payload (`MaterialComplexity`, `SampleStructure`, `PolarizerBehavior`, `SourceTuning`) is bound by the serializer, which reports a malformed one as `MalformedJsonErr`. A file of another version therefore passes the schema and reaches the typed version check. Each file is a `Content` item copied `PreserveNewest`, beside the existing `schema/optical-constructor-*.schema.json` items of `OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj`, with no new comment. (3) `SchemaValidation.fs` gains `type LibraryEntryKind with member schemaFile : FileName` (`schema/library-<kind>.schema.json`); the common schema and one lazy per kind, each loaded once (`JsonSchema.FromText` registers an `$id` only once, `:17-21`), with the common schema loaded before any entry schema evaluates; and `validateEntry (kind : LibraryEntryKind) (element : JsonElement)` over step 29's `validateWith`. (4) New `OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs`, `module EntryFileJson`, compiled directly after `CanonicalJson.fs`. `LibraryFileText of string` is a library file's text, UTF-8 without a BOM; S2's database payload and S4's kit snapshot hold it byte for byte. `LibraryEntryContent.sealed : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, StorageError>` is the content with `contentHashOf content` (step 27). `LibraryEntryEnvelope.fileText : Result<LibraryFileText, StorageError>` is the content's canonical node with `contentHash` added beside its keys, rendered indented and ending with one `\\n`; `ProjectJson.serializeProject` adds `schemaVersion` the same way. `LibraryFileText.parseEntry (kind : LibraryEntryKind) : Result<LibraryEntryEnvelope, StorageError>` works in this order. It parses the text (`MalformedJsonErr`). It validates the document against the kind's schema (`SchemaValidationErr`), so a file of another kind fails here. It compares `schema.version` with `kind.currentSchemaVersion` before anything binds (`UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`). It binds the content from the document without `contentHash` (`MalformedJsonErr`). Finally it compares `contentHashOf content` with the recorded hash (`ContentHashMismatchErr`). There are no up-converters and no fallback readers. Every .NET call that throws is caught here and mapped; nothing above handles an exception. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs` (`module EntryFileJsonTests`), appended to the compile list after `LibraryEntryFilesTests.fs`. Each round trip goes content → `sealed` → `fileText` → `parseEntry` and answers an equal envelope, whose decoder answers the original value. (a) `a material entry file round-trips every complexity shape`: one constant complexity for each `ConstantEpsValue` case; dispersive complexities over `IsotropicDispersive`, `UniaxialDispersive` and `BiaxialDispersive` whose segments together carry every `EpsAxisDispersion` case: `RealNK` (through `DispersionModel.toEpsAxis` of a Cauchy model) and `ComplexEps` (of a Sellmeier model), `TabulatedNK` (through `TabulatedNkTable.tryCreate`), `TaucLorentzAxis`, `GaussianOscillatorAxis`, `ForouhiBloomerAxis` and `BrendelBormannAxis` (through `toEpsAxis` of coefficient sets written in the fixture), and `PublishedLawAxis` of each `PublishedIndexLaw`; one complexity with a constant and one with a dispersive `magnetic` aspect; and one with each `active` case, `RhoWithoutDispValue`, `RhoWithDispValue` and `PublishedLawRho LangasiteGyrationLaw`. (b) `a multilayer sample entry file round-trips`: `SeedSamples.multilayerQw` (a `Repeated` period group) and `SeedSamples.langasiteSilicon`. (c) `a tunable source entry file round-trips`: a `SeedSources.tunables` source under `BuiltInProvenance` and a user source under `UserProvenance`. (d) `a constant-Mueller polarizer entry file round-trips`: a two-component `ConstantMueller` polarizer in the `CustomMueller` category. (e) `a detector and a category entry file round-trip`: the ellipsometer detector and the `standardCategories` Vacuum category. (f) `every provenance round-trips through an entry file`: one material under each of the four provenance cases. (g) `an entry file is indented canonical JSON whose hash survives a write and a read`: the text is the indented canonical rendering, ends with one `\\n` and holds no `\\r`; writing the parsed envelope again gives the same text; and the hash equals `contentHashOf` of the content. (h) `an entry file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: a material file with `schema.version` set to 2 answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = MaterialEntryKind.extension`, `found = FileSchemaVersion 2` and `expected = FileSchemaVersion 1`, both with its body intact and with `payload` replaced by `{}`. (i) `a tampered entry file is ContentHashMismatchErr`: a number inside the payload changed in the text, with the recorded hash kept, answers `ContentHashMismatchErr` whose `recorded` is the file's hash and whose `computed` is the changed content's. (j) `a schema-invalid or wrong-kind entry file is SchemaValidationErr`: the file without `name`, and a sample's file parsed as a material, answer `SchemaValidationErr` with messages; a text that is not JSON answers `MalformedJsonErr`.", "acceptance": "After the entry files land, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including the ten EntryFileJsonTests facts from `a material entry file round-trips every complexity shape` to `a schema-invalid or wrong-kind entry file is SchemaValidationErr`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/Errors.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-common.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-material.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-sample.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-source.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-polarizer.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-detector.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-category.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/OpticalConstructor.Tests.fsproj"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a material entry file round-trips every complexity shape", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a multilayer sample entry file round-trips", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a tunable source entry file round-trips", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a constant-Mueller polarizer entry file round-trips", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a detector and a category entry file round-trip", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.every provenance round-trips through an entry file", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.an entry file is indented canonical JSON whose hash survives a write and a read", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.an entry file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a tampered entry file is ContentHashMismatchErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid or wrong-kind entry file is SchemaValidationErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-ENTRY-FILES"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
{"number": 31, "anchor": "IMPLEMENT", "ac": "AC-S1.4j", "touches": ["OpticalConstructor.Storage", "OpticalConstructor.Tests"], "depends_on": [30], "how_to": "The catalogue manifest's file, and the proof that every built-in has a file form (001 §A; 001 §B; .spec-md §5). (1) `schema/library-catalogue.schema.json` has its own `$id` and references `library-common.schema.json`. `schemaVersion` is a positive integer, checked unconditionally. Under `if` it is 1: `id` a GUID, `name` a non-empty string, `version` positive, `entries` an array of rows `{ kind: 1 to 6, id, version, fileName: a non-empty string, contentHash }`, and no other key. It is a `Content` item like step 30's. `SchemaValidation.validateCatalogueManifest (element : JsonElement)` runs over `validateWith`, with its schema loaded once. (2) `EntryFileJson.fs` gains three members. `CatalogueManifest.fileText : Result<LibraryFileText, StorageError>` is indented canonical text ending with one `\\n`. `CatalogueManifest.manifestHash : Result<ContentHash, StorageError>` is `contentHashOf` the manifest, the hash S3's start-up import compares (001 §B 'Import on every start'). `LibraryFileText.parseCatalogueManifest : Result<CatalogueManifest, StorageError>` parses (`MalformedJsonErr`), validates (`SchemaValidationErr`), compares `schemaVersion` with `CatalogueManifest.currentSchemaVersion` (`UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = CatalogueManifest.extension`, step 26), and binds (`MalformedJsonErr`). (3) The built-ins: the code seeds are still present (`builtInEntries`, `standardCategories` and `seedEntries`, which S1.7 deletes). Every one of them is sealed at version 1 under `BuiltInProvenance` of a test catalogue id, written, parsed and decoded. Tests, in `EntryFileJsonTests`: (a) `a catalogue manifest round-trips and its hash is stable`: a manifest from `CatalogueManifest.tryCreate` over sealed envelopes of three kinds, written and parsed, is equal; its `manifestHash` is equal before and after and equals `contentHashOf` of the manifest; and changing one row's hash changes it. (b) `a catalogue manifest of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: with `schemaVersion` set to 2, it answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `CatalogueManifest.extension`, found 2 and expected 1. (c) `a schema-invalid catalogue manifest is SchemaValidationErr`: a row without `contentHash` answers `SchemaValidationErr`. (d) `every built-in seals, writes, reads and decodes equal to its seed`: every `builtInEntries` material, every `standardCategories` category and every `seedEntries` sample, source, detector and polarizer round-trips through its entry file, and its decoder answers a value equal to the seed. (e) `the built-ins form one catalogue with unique file names per kind`: `CatalogueManifest.tryCreate` over all of their envelopes is `Ok`, so the built-ins' file names are unique per kind and no id and version repeats; it has one row per built-in, and the manifest round-trips.", "acceptance": "After the catalogue file lands, constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a catalogue manifest round-trips and its hash is stable`, `a catalogue manifest of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid catalogue manifest is SchemaValidationErr`, `every built-in seals, writes, reads and decodes equal to its seed` and `the built-ins form one catalogue with unique file names per kind`; and build, elevation, constructor-unit-tests and the six s04 invariants MUST pass.", "required_gates": ["build", "elevation", "constructor-unit-tests"], "gate_selection": {"constructor-unit-tests": {"mode": "all_discovered", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests"}}, "effects": {"edits": ["Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/EntryFileJson.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/SchemaValidation.fs", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/schema/library-catalogue.schema.json", "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs"], "tests": [{"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a catalogue manifest round-trips and its hash is stable", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CATALOGUE-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a catalogue manifest of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CATALOGUE-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.a schema-invalid catalogue manifest is SchemaValidationErr", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CATALOGUE-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.every built-in seals, writes, reads and decodes equal to its seed", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CATALOGUE-FILE"]}, {"op": "create", "suite": "constructor-unit-tests", "id": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests.the built-ins form one catalogue with unique file names per kind", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Tests/EntryFileJsonTests.fs", "class": "OpticalConstructor.Tests.EntryFileJsonTests", "discovery_gate": "constructor-unit-tests", "obligations": ["S14-CATALOGUE-FILE"]}], "contracts": [], "packages": [], "checks": []}, "section": "S1.4 -- Library entry files: envelope, provenance, canonical JSON, content hash, schemas"}
